1
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:10,140
Today, we're looking
at some of the hottest weather...

2
00:05:04,881 --> 00:05:06,051
Hey.

3
00:05:10,681 --> 00:05:11,681
What is it?

4
00:05:14,101 --> 00:05:15,391
What?

5
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:18,691
We've been ordered to stand down.
They're scrapping the program.

6
00:05:19,941 --> 00:05:21,941
They say we fell short.

7
00:05:22,031 --> 00:05:24,241
The contract threshold is Mach 10.

8
00:05:24,321 --> 00:05:28,451
Mach 10 is supposed to be in two months.
Today's test point is Mach 9.

9
00:05:28,531 --> 00:05:30,371
Well, that's not good enough.

10
00:05:30,451 --> 00:05:31,831
Says who?

11
00:05:31,911 --> 00:05:33,451
Admiral Cain.

12
00:05:34,751 --> 00:05:36,211
The Drone Ranger.

13
00:05:36,291 --> 00:05:38,791
He wants our budget
for his unmanned program.

14
00:05:38,881 --> 00:05:42,381
He's on his way to kill the test
and shut us down personally.

15
00:05:56,101 --> 00:05:57,691
Well, he isn't here yet.

16
00:06:01,941 --> 00:06:03,281
They want Mach 10,

17
00:06:03,981 --> 00:06:05,191
let's give 'em Mach 10.

18
00:06:23,211 --> 00:06:26,131
Now remember,
the contract threshold is Mach 10.

19
00:06:26,221 --> 00:06:29,721
Not 10.1. Not 10.2. Mach 10.

20
00:06:29,801 --> 00:06:31,801
That should keep the program alive.

21
00:06:34,721 --> 00:06:36,271
I don't like that look, Mav.

22
00:06:38,311 --> 00:06:39,811
It's the only one I got.

23
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:51,371
Control, this is Darkstar.
How do you read?

24
00:06:51,451 --> 00:06:53,831
Darkstar, Control. Loud and clear. How me?

25
00:06:53,911 --> 00:06:55,871
Loud and clear.
Takeoff precheck's complete.

26
00:06:55,951 --> 00:06:57,161
Ready for APU start.

27
00:06:58,121 --> 00:06:59,921
Ready left engine start.

28
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:03,131
Ready right engine start.

29
00:07:04,251 --> 00:07:05,341
Thumbs for taxi.

30
00:07:07,841 --> 00:07:09,511
We are ready for taxi.

31
00:07:11,131 --> 00:07:14,511
Tower, this is Darkstar.
We are taxiing with information Alpha.

32
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:16,521
Darkstar, you are clear to taxi.

33
00:07:16,601 --> 00:07:19,521
Runway 21. Winds 210, 10.

34
00:07:19,601 --> 00:07:22,101
-Fuel temps are looking good.
-Control concurs.

35
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:24,861
Battery's holding at 95%.
Cabin pressure looks good.

36
00:07:24,941 --> 00:07:26,151
Control concurs.

37
00:07:26,231 --> 00:07:27,861
Tower, this is Darkstar.
We're ready for takeoff.

38
00:07:27,941 --> 00:07:30,901
Requesting an unrestricted climb
to 600 and above.

39
00:07:30,991 --> 00:07:33,411
Darkstar, the runway and skies are yours.

40
00:07:33,491 --> 00:07:35,531
Rear Admiral Chester Cain.

41
00:07:36,291 --> 00:07:38,871
Maverick, Cain just pulled up to the gate.

42
00:07:39,621 --> 00:07:41,041
It's not too late to stop, buddy.

43
00:07:42,121 --> 00:07:44,751
You know what happens to you
if you go through with this.

44
00:07:46,921 --> 00:07:49,381
I know what happens
to everyone else if I don't.

45
00:07:51,681 --> 00:07:53,641
Darkstar is ready for takeoff.

46
00:07:56,641 --> 00:07:57,761
Everyone,

47
00:07:58,271 --> 00:08:00,521
go for takeoff, starting with engine.

48
00:08:00,601 --> 00:08:02,391
-Engine, go.
-Thermals, go.

49
00:08:02,481 --> 00:08:04,561
-Fuel, go.
-Electric, go.

50
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:05,981
Control surfaces, go.

51
00:08:06,061 --> 00:08:08,781
Darkstar, Control.
You're cleared for takeoff.

52
00:08:08,861 --> 00:08:10,401
All right, sweetheart,

53
00:08:11,071 --> 00:08:12,241
one last ride.

54
00:08:37,971 --> 00:08:41,981
Darkstar, you are cleared above 600.
Increase to Mach 3.5.

55
00:08:42,061 --> 00:08:45,902
Cleared above 600. Increase to Mach 3.5.

56
00:08:52,242 --> 00:08:53,282
Admiral.

57
00:08:54,072 --> 00:08:56,622
-Just in time, sir.
-I'm early. So are you.

58
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:58,162
You care to explain?

59
00:08:58,242 --> 00:09:00,202
Transitioning to scramjet.

60
00:09:14,592 --> 00:09:16,012
Mav, Admiral Cain is asking--

61
00:09:16,092 --> 00:09:18,552
-Ordering.
-Ordering that we bring her down.

62
00:09:26,142 --> 00:09:27,602
...within six...

63
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,442
This is where we've had trouble
with comms, sir.

64
00:09:29,522 --> 00:09:31,902
It's the Earth's curvature.
It's called "Earth Bulge."

65
00:09:31,982 --> 00:09:33,322
Did anyone offer you a coffee?

66
00:09:35,072 --> 00:09:35,902
Okay.

67
00:09:43,872 --> 00:09:45,752
He's at Mach 7, pushing 8.

68
00:09:45,832 --> 00:09:48,042
-Flight data?
-Receiving. Data is good.

69
00:09:53,422 --> 00:09:55,802
Temperature's climbing.
Response is still stable.

70
00:09:55,882 --> 00:09:56,722
We're feeling good.

71
00:10:00,512 --> 00:10:01,722
Mach 8.8.

72
00:10:02,722 --> 00:10:03,722
8.9.

73
00:10:04,352 --> 00:10:05,642
Mach 9.

74
00:10:05,732 --> 00:10:07,442
He's the fastest man alive.

75
00:10:26,712 --> 00:10:28,332
Talk to me, Goose.

76
00:10:30,332 --> 00:10:31,462
Mach 9.1.

77
00:10:32,462 --> 00:10:33,462
9.2.

78
00:10:40,762 --> 00:10:41,972
Mach 9.3.

79
00:10:44,682 --> 00:10:45,892
9.4.

80
00:10:47,392 --> 00:10:49,352
Approaching high hypersonic.

81
00:11:01,742 --> 00:11:03,282
Windshield hot caution.

82
00:11:12,422 --> 00:11:14,042
Surface temp rising.

83
00:11:19,422 --> 00:11:21,392
Come on, sweetheart, just a little more.

84
00:11:22,222 --> 00:11:23,262
Just a little.

85
00:11:27,062 --> 00:11:27,932
Come on!

86
00:11:34,572 --> 00:11:35,402
Come on!

87
00:11:40,902 --> 00:11:41,912
Mach 10!

88
00:11:44,582 --> 00:11:46,412
Put that in your Pentagon budget!

89
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:49,542
Sir.

90
00:12:01,132 --> 00:12:02,342
Don't do it. Don't do it.

91
00:12:02,432 --> 00:12:03,432
Just...

92
00:12:05,352 --> 00:12:07,512
a little push.

93
00:12:11,642 --> 00:12:13,402
Holy shit.

94
00:12:22,862 --> 00:12:25,912
You got some balls, stick jockey.

95
00:12:25,992 --> 00:12:27,413
I'll give you that.

96
00:12:31,663 --> 00:12:32,833
Oh, shit.

97
00:12:38,253 --> 00:12:39,133
Maverick.

98
00:12:41,173 --> 00:12:42,473
Maverick!

99
00:13:32,723 --> 00:13:33,813
Thank you.

100
00:13:34,643 --> 00:13:35,813
Where am I?

101
00:13:37,273 --> 00:13:38,483
Earth.

102
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:54,413
Maverick.

103
00:13:55,163 --> 00:13:56,833
Thirty-plus years of service.

104
00:13:58,043 --> 00:13:59,423
Combat medals.

105
00:13:59,503 --> 00:14:00,843
Citations.

106
00:14:01,503 --> 00:14:05,923
Only man to shoot down three enemy planes
in the last 40 years.

107
00:14:06,593 --> 00:14:07,973
"Distinguished."

108
00:14:08,053 --> 00:14:11,643
"Distinguished." "Distinguished."

109
00:14:13,393 --> 00:14:16,693
Yet you can't get a promotion,
you won't retire,

110
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:19,813
and despite your best efforts,
you refuse to die.

111
00:14:20,403 --> 00:14:24,443
You should be at least a two-star admiral
by now, if not a senator.

112
00:14:24,993 --> 00:14:26,613
Yet here you are:

113
00:14:28,283 --> 00:14:29,363
Captain.

114
00:14:30,453 --> 00:14:31,783
Why is that?

115
00:14:32,583 --> 00:14:34,203
It's one of life's mysteries, sir.

116
00:14:34,293 --> 00:14:37,793
This isn't a joke. I asked you a question.

117
00:14:39,633 --> 00:14:41,463
I'm where I belong, sir.

118
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:44,673
Well, the navy doesn't see it that way.

119
00:14:45,713 --> 00:14:46,803
Not anymore.

120
00:14:48,303 --> 00:14:50,013
These planes you've been testing,

121
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:51,803
Captain,

122
00:14:52,353 --> 00:14:55,353
one day, sooner than later,
they won't need pilots at all.

123
00:14:56,103 --> 00:14:59,443
Pilots that need to sleep, eat,
take a piss.

124
00:15:01,653 --> 00:15:03,823
Pilots that disobey orders.

125
00:15:05,283 --> 00:15:08,203
All you did was buy some time
for those men out there.

126
00:15:10,283 --> 00:15:11,533
The future is coming,

127
00:15:12,573 --> 00:15:14,413
and you're not in it.

128
00:15:16,333 --> 00:15:18,413
Escort this man off the base.

129
00:15:19,583 --> 00:15:23,923
Take him to his quarters.
Wait with him while he packs his gear.

130
00:15:26,263 --> 00:15:29,383
I want him on the road to North Island
within the hour.

131
00:15:32,643 --> 00:15:34,183
North Island, sir?

132
00:15:35,143 --> 00:15:37,603
Call came in with impeccable timing,

133
00:15:37,683 --> 00:15:41,353
right as I was driving here
to ground your ass once and for all.

134
00:15:42,813 --> 00:15:45,363
It galls me to say it, but...

135
00:15:46,783 --> 00:15:50,533
for reasons known only to the Almighty
and your guardian angel...

136
00:15:52,533 --> 00:15:54,953
you've been called back to TOPGUN.

137
00:15:59,123 --> 00:16:02,543
-Sir?
-You are dismissed, Captain.

138
00:16:07,803 --> 00:16:09,723
The end is inevitable, Maverick.

139
00:16:10,633 --> 00:16:12,554
Your kind is headed for extinction.

140
00:16:16,354 --> 00:16:17,854
Maybe so, sir.

141
00:16:19,524 --> 00:16:20,984
But not today.

142
00:17:26,044 --> 00:17:28,754
Captain Pete "Maverick" Mitchell.

143
00:17:29,554 --> 00:17:31,424
Your reputation precedes you.

144
00:17:32,714 --> 00:17:33,764
Thank you, sir.

145
00:17:35,094 --> 00:17:36,554
Wasn't a compliment.

146
00:17:38,354 --> 00:17:39,354
I'm Admiral Beau Simpson.

147
00:17:39,434 --> 00:17:41,604
I'm the Air Boss.
I believe you know Admiral Bates.

148
00:17:42,354 --> 00:17:43,314
Warlock, sir.

149
00:17:43,354 --> 00:17:46,104
Must admit,
I wasn't expecting an invitation back.

150
00:17:46,194 --> 00:17:47,984
They're called orders, Maverick.

151
00:17:49,364 --> 00:17:50,864
You two have something in common.

152
00:17:50,944 --> 00:17:53,744
Cyclone here was first in his class
back in '88.

153
00:17:53,824 --> 00:17:55,784
Actually, sir, I finished second.

154
00:17:56,454 --> 00:17:58,454
Just want to manage expectations.

155
00:18:02,664 --> 00:18:03,914
The target...

156
00:18:06,044 --> 00:18:08,754
is an unsanctioned
uranium enrichment plant

157
00:18:08,834 --> 00:18:11,304
built in violation
of a multilateral NATO treaty.

158
00:18:11,384 --> 00:18:14,344
The uranium produced there
represents a direct threat

159
00:18:14,424 --> 00:18:15,724
to our allies in the region.

160
00:18:15,804 --> 00:18:20,054
The Pentagon has tasked us with assembling
a strike team and taking it out

161
00:18:20,144 --> 00:18:21,854
before it becomes fully operational.

162
00:18:22,894 --> 00:18:26,734
The plant sits in an underground bunker
at the end of this valley.

163
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:28,524
Said valley is GPS-jammed

164
00:18:28,604 --> 00:18:31,404
and defended by an extensive
surface-to-air missile array

165
00:18:31,484 --> 00:18:34,154
serving a limited number
of fifth-generation fighters,

166
00:18:34,234 --> 00:18:38,204
which in turn are backed up by
a plentiful reserve of surplus aircraft.

167
00:18:38,284 --> 00:18:40,574
Even a few old F-14s.

168
00:18:40,664 --> 00:18:42,954
Seems like we're not the only ones
holding on to old relics.

169
00:18:44,794 --> 00:18:46,254
What's your read, Captain?

170
00:18:48,424 --> 00:18:52,214
Well, sir, normally this would be
a cakewalk for the F-35's stealth,

171
00:18:52,294 --> 00:18:55,014
but the GPS-jamming negates that.

172
00:18:55,094 --> 00:18:58,844
And a surface-to-air threat necessitates
a low-level laser-guided strike

173
00:18:58,934 --> 00:19:00,344
tailor-made for the F-18.

174
00:19:00,434 --> 00:19:01,434
I figure,

175
00:19:02,104 --> 00:19:04,104
two precision bombs, minimum.

176
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:06,644
Makes it four aircraft flying in pairs.

177
00:19:07,184 --> 00:19:09,394
That is one hell of a steep climb
out of there,

178
00:19:09,484 --> 00:19:11,814
exposing you
to all the surface-to-air missiles.

179
00:19:12,524 --> 00:19:13,774
You survive that,

180
00:19:15,034 --> 00:19:16,654
it's a dogfight all the way home.

181
00:19:16,744 --> 00:19:19,364
All requirements for which
you have real-world experience.

182
00:19:20,114 --> 00:19:22,204
Not in the same mission, sir.

183
00:19:24,954 --> 00:19:25,954
No.

184
00:19:28,794 --> 00:19:31,254
No, someone's not coming back from this.

185
00:19:31,334 --> 00:19:32,794
Can it be done or not?

186
00:19:33,464 --> 00:19:35,304
How soon before the plant
becomes operational?

187
00:19:35,384 --> 00:19:37,174
Three weeks. Maybe less.

188
00:19:38,554 --> 00:19:41,184
Well, it's been a while
since I've flown an F-18, and...

189
00:19:42,184 --> 00:19:44,644
I'm not sure who I'd trust
to fly the other three.

190
00:19:44,724 --> 00:19:46,854
But I'll find a way to make it work.

191
00:19:46,934 --> 00:19:48,604
I think you misunderstand, Captain.

192
00:19:49,314 --> 00:19:50,144
Sir?

193
00:19:50,234 --> 00:19:53,484
We don't want you to fly it.
We want you to teach it.

194
00:19:56,404 --> 00:19:57,694
Teach, sir?

195
00:19:59,244 --> 00:20:02,744
We've recalled 12 TOPGUN graduates
from their squadrons.

196
00:20:02,824 --> 00:20:05,534
We want you to narrow that pool
down to six.

197
00:20:06,204 --> 00:20:07,794
They'll fly the mission.

198
00:20:09,504 --> 00:20:10,914
Is there a problem, Captain?

199
00:20:12,834 --> 00:20:15,134
You know there is, sir.

200
00:20:16,344 --> 00:20:17,174
Yeah.

201
00:20:17,844 --> 00:20:20,344
Bradley Bradshaw, aka "Rooster."

202
00:20:20,424 --> 00:20:22,264
I understand you used to fly
with his old man.

203
00:20:22,344 --> 00:20:24,144
What was his call sign?

204
00:20:24,894 --> 00:20:26,514
"Goose," sir.

205
00:20:26,604 --> 00:20:27,934
Tragic what happened.

206
00:20:28,024 --> 00:20:29,934
Captain Mitchell was cleared
of any wrongdoing.

207
00:20:30,024 --> 00:20:31,854
Goose's death was an accident.

208
00:20:31,944 --> 00:20:33,564
Is that how you see it, Captain?

209
00:20:33,654 --> 00:20:35,734
Is that how Goose's son sees it?

210
00:20:38,784 --> 00:20:41,744
With all due respect, sir,
I'm not a teacher.

211
00:20:41,824 --> 00:20:43,494
You were a TOPGUN instructor before.

212
00:20:43,574 --> 00:20:45,994
That was almost 30 years ago.
I lasted two months.

213
00:20:46,074 --> 00:20:47,334
It's not where I belong.

214
00:20:47,414 --> 00:20:49,584
Then let me be perfectly blunt.

215
00:20:49,664 --> 00:20:52,924
You were not my first choice.
In fact, you weren't even on the list.

216
00:20:53,714 --> 00:20:56,254
You are here at the request
of Admiral Kazansky.

217
00:20:56,964 --> 00:21:00,634
Now, Iceman happens to be a man
I deeply admire,

218
00:21:00,714 --> 00:21:03,724
and he seems to think that you have
something left to offer the navy.

219
00:21:04,724 --> 00:21:06,644
What that is, I can't imagine.

220
00:21:08,104 --> 00:21:09,974
You don't have to take this job.

221
00:21:10,064 --> 00:21:11,314
But let me be clear:

222
00:21:11,394 --> 00:21:14,314
This will be your last post, Captain.

223
00:21:16,064 --> 00:21:19,534
You fly for TOPGUN,
or you don't fly for the navy ever again.

224
00:21:28,084 --> 00:21:29,914
Twenty bucks you can't get three in a row.

225
00:22:11,333 --> 00:22:13,543
Oh, you've got to be kidding me.

226
00:22:16,123 --> 00:22:17,213
Pete.

227
00:22:18,583 --> 00:22:19,713
Penny?

228
00:22:20,673 --> 00:22:24,093
-What are you doing here?
-I should ask you the same thing.

229
00:22:25,343 --> 00:22:27,553
-Well, that is a long story.
-I doubt that.

230
00:22:27,633 --> 00:22:28,473
Yeah.

231
00:22:28,553 --> 00:22:30,353
Who'd you piss off this time?

232
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:31,853
Another admiral.

233
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:32,933
Exactly.

234
00:22:35,773 --> 00:22:37,813
-Are you mad at me?
-Oh, Pete.

235
00:22:38,773 --> 00:22:41,943
I can never stay mad at you.
That's the problem.

236
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:44,693
I got to say,

237
00:22:44,783 --> 00:22:48,323
North Island is the one place
I thought for sure I'd never run into you.

238
00:22:48,823 --> 00:22:51,783
-How long you been here?
-Bought this place about three years ago.

239
00:22:51,873 --> 00:22:53,703
-Three years?
-Yeah.

240
00:22:53,793 --> 00:22:58,293
Not long after you got shipped off to the
desert for pissing off that other admiral.

241
00:22:59,213 --> 00:23:01,343
That was three years ago?

242
00:23:02,463 --> 00:23:04,633
You must be in a lot of trouble.

243
00:23:05,213 --> 00:23:07,303
No way you'd come back here willingly.

244
00:23:09,133 --> 00:23:10,143
Well,

245
00:23:10,973 --> 00:23:12,553
you'll sort it out.

246
00:23:13,223 --> 00:23:14,433
No, I think...

247
00:23:15,813 --> 00:23:18,313
-I think this is it.
-Come on, Pete.

248
00:23:18,393 --> 00:23:21,153
You've been saying that
as long as I've known you.

249
00:23:21,233 --> 00:23:24,863
You said it after they busted you for
taking me on a joyride in that F-18.

250
00:23:25,443 --> 00:23:27,863
Then the next thing I know,
you're off to Bosnia.

251
00:23:28,493 --> 00:23:31,073
Then Iraq. Both times.

252
00:23:31,163 --> 00:23:32,783
You get yourself in trouble,

253
00:23:33,913 --> 00:23:36,793
Iceman makes a call,
and you're back in the air.

254
00:23:36,873 --> 00:23:38,413
Penny, this is different.

255
00:23:38,503 --> 00:23:40,003
Pete, trust me,

256
00:23:40,083 --> 00:23:42,333
as improbable as it seems right now,

257
00:23:42,423 --> 00:23:45,753
somehow you'll be back in a fighter plane
with your tail on fire.

258
00:23:46,923 --> 00:23:48,923
-Penny...
-Too late.

259
00:23:49,013 --> 00:23:49,843
What?

260
00:23:49,933 --> 00:23:52,093
You were about to ask me
what time I get off.

261
00:23:55,683 --> 00:23:57,353
Don't give me that look.

262
00:23:58,523 --> 00:24:00,983
I'm not giving you any look. I swear.

263
00:24:01,693 --> 00:24:04,193
It always ends the same with us, Pete.

264
00:24:05,693 --> 00:24:07,533
Let's not start this time.

265
00:24:11,953 --> 00:24:12,783
Okay.

266
00:24:13,703 --> 00:24:14,703
Okay.

267
00:24:19,543 --> 00:24:20,873
You look good.

268
00:24:31,053 --> 00:24:32,633
Much appreciated, pal.

269
00:24:35,393 --> 00:24:36,473
What am I missing?

270
00:24:38,893 --> 00:24:42,813
"Disrespect a lady, the navy,
or put your cell phone on my bar..."

271
00:24:42,903 --> 00:24:44,773
"...and you buy a round."

272
00:24:45,363 --> 00:24:46,483
For everyone?

273
00:24:46,573 --> 00:24:49,323
I'm afraid rules are rules.
You're lucky it's early.

274
00:24:50,533 --> 00:24:52,153
Oh, come on!

275
00:24:52,743 --> 00:24:54,703
What do we have here?

276
00:24:56,413 --> 00:24:58,663
If it ain't Phoenix!

277
00:24:58,743 --> 00:25:01,163
And here I thought we were special,
Coyote.

278
00:25:02,583 --> 00:25:05,463
Turns out the invite went to anyone.

279
00:25:06,253 --> 00:25:07,883
Fellas, this here's Bagman.

280
00:25:07,963 --> 00:25:09,713
-Hangman.
-Whatever.

281
00:25:10,263 --> 00:25:12,513
You're looking at the only naval aviator
on active duty

282
00:25:12,593 --> 00:25:14,093
with a confirmed air-to-air kill.

283
00:25:14,183 --> 00:25:15,013
Stop.

284
00:25:15,093 --> 00:25:19,103
Mind you, the other guy was in
a museum piece from the Korean War.

285
00:25:19,183 --> 00:25:21,933
-Cold War.
-Different wars, same century.

286
00:25:22,023 --> 00:25:23,023
Not this one.

287
00:25:23,103 --> 00:25:24,483
Who are your friends?

288
00:25:24,563 --> 00:25:26,563
-Payback.
-Fanboy.

289
00:25:26,653 --> 00:25:28,653
-Hey, Coyote.
-Hey.

290
00:25:28,733 --> 00:25:30,283
-Who's he?
-Who's who?

291
00:25:33,363 --> 00:25:34,663
When did you get in?

292
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:37,373
I've been here the whole time.

293
00:25:38,033 --> 00:25:40,083
-The man's a stealth pilot.
-Literally.

294
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:42,543
Weapons systems officer, actually.

295
00:25:43,213 --> 00:25:44,623
With no sense of humor.

296
00:25:46,583 --> 00:25:47,753
What do they call you?

297
00:25:48,463 --> 00:25:49,803
Bob.

298
00:25:49,883 --> 00:25:51,133
No, your call sign.

299
00:25:54,053 --> 00:25:55,053
Bob.

300
00:25:55,553 --> 00:25:56,473
Bob Floyd.

301
00:25:57,343 --> 00:26:00,183
You're my new backseater? From Lemoore?

302
00:26:01,353 --> 00:26:03,063
Looks like it. Yeah.

303
00:26:06,653 --> 00:26:07,983
Nine-ball, Bob.

304
00:26:08,733 --> 00:26:09,573
Rack 'em.

305
00:26:11,573 --> 00:26:12,823
Okay.

306
00:26:13,493 --> 00:26:15,493
-Penny, my dear.
-Yeah.

307
00:26:15,573 --> 00:26:17,743
I'll have four more on the old-timer.

308
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,093
Bradshaw!

309
00:26:36,843 --> 00:26:38,343
Is that you?

310
00:26:43,973 --> 00:26:46,063
This is how I find out you're stateside?

311
00:26:46,193 --> 00:26:48,063
Yeah, I just thought I'd surprise you.

312
00:26:50,863 --> 00:26:52,983
I guess I surprised you back.

313
00:26:54,692 --> 00:26:56,492
-It's good to see you.
-Good to see you too.

314
00:26:59,202 --> 00:27:00,952
-Here you go.
-Thank you.

315
00:27:01,032 --> 00:27:02,742
Much appreciated, Pops.

316
00:27:10,212 --> 00:27:13,052
How about ringing me up
before the evening rush?

317
00:27:27,182 --> 00:27:28,442
Bradshaw.

318
00:27:28,522 --> 00:27:30,102
As I live and breathe.

319
00:27:30,942 --> 00:27:31,942
Hangman.

320
00:27:32,022 --> 00:27:34,192
You look... good.

321
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:37,112
Well, I am good, Rooster.

322
00:27:38,952 --> 00:27:39,952
I'm very good.

323
00:27:40,532 --> 00:27:42,072
In fact,

324
00:27:42,162 --> 00:27:43,952
I am too good to be true.

325
00:27:44,032 --> 00:27:45,292
So,

326
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:47,912
anybody know what this special
detachment is all about?

327
00:27:48,002 --> 00:27:51,042
No, mission's a mission.
They don't confront me.

328
00:27:51,792 --> 00:27:54,752
What I want to know:
Who's gonna be team leader?

329
00:27:55,462 --> 00:27:59,472
And which one of y'all has what it takes
to follow me?

330
00:28:00,972 --> 00:28:04,472
Hangman, the only place you'll lead anyone
is an early grave.

331
00:28:13,312 --> 00:28:17,072
Well, anyone who follows you
is just gonna run out of fuel.

332
00:28:17,902 --> 00:28:20,202
But that's just you, ain't it, Rooster?

333
00:28:20,992 --> 00:28:23,492
You're snug on that perch,

334
00:28:23,572 --> 00:28:25,782
waiting for just the right moment...

335
00:28:27,912 --> 00:28:29,252
that never comes.

336
00:28:41,722 --> 00:28:43,392
Well, he hasn't changed.

337
00:28:44,432 --> 00:28:46,602
Nope. Sure hasn't.

338
00:28:51,192 --> 00:28:52,232
Check it out.

339
00:28:53,311 --> 00:28:54,441
More patches.

340
00:28:54,981 --> 00:28:58,071
That's Harvard, Yale, Omaha.
Shit, that's Fritz.

341
00:28:58,151 --> 00:29:00,361
What the hell kind of mission is this?

342
00:29:01,361 --> 00:29:03,361
That's not the question
we should be asking.

343
00:29:04,161 --> 00:29:06,161
Everyone here is the best there is.

344
00:29:07,661 --> 00:29:09,621
Who the hell are they gonna get
to teach us?

345
00:29:13,041 --> 00:29:14,581
It's been declined.

346
00:29:15,171 --> 00:29:16,001
You're kidding.

347
00:29:31,681 --> 00:29:33,941
Hey, guys. Come on.

348
00:29:48,031 --> 00:29:49,081
How about...

349
00:29:50,621 --> 00:29:52,371
That won't cover it.

350
00:29:57,841 --> 00:30:00,341
I'll come by tomorrow
and bring you the cash.

351
00:30:00,421 --> 00:30:03,301
I'm afraid rules are rules, Pete.

352
00:30:09,391 --> 00:30:12,271
Overboard! Overboard!

353
00:30:13,181 --> 00:30:14,431
Really?

354
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:18,561
Overboard! Overboard!

355
00:30:25,781 --> 00:30:27,661
Great to see you, Pete!

356
00:30:28,321 --> 00:30:31,161
Overboard! Overboard!

357
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:37,171
Thanks for the beers! Come back anytime!

358
00:31:39,230 --> 00:31:42,310
Altitude 8,000... 7,000...

359
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:44,730
Goose, I can't reach the ejection handle.

360
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:46,820
Eject, eject, eject!

361
00:31:52,740 --> 00:31:54,240
Goose! Oh, no!

362
00:31:54,330 --> 00:31:57,120
God, he loved flying with you, Maverick.

363
00:32:41,210 --> 00:32:42,420
Attention on deck!

364
00:32:53,339 --> 00:32:54,389
Morning.

365
00:32:55,049 --> 00:32:57,219
Welcome to your special training
detachment.

366
00:32:57,309 --> 00:32:58,349
Be seated.

367
00:32:58,929 --> 00:33:01,599
I'm Admiral Bates, NAWDC commander.

368
00:33:01,689 --> 00:33:03,439
You're all TOPGUN graduates.

369
00:33:04,229 --> 00:33:05,519
The elite.

370
00:33:05,609 --> 00:33:07,609
The best of the best.

371
00:33:08,189 --> 00:33:10,029
That was yesterday.

372
00:33:11,069 --> 00:33:15,069
The enemy's new fifth-generation fighter
has leveled the playing field.

373
00:33:15,159 --> 00:33:16,779
Details are few, but you can be sure

374
00:33:16,869 --> 00:33:18,909
we no longer possess
the technological advantage.

375
00:33:18,989 --> 00:33:22,289
Success, now more than ever,

376
00:33:22,369 --> 00:33:25,539
comes down to the man or woman in the box.

377
00:33:26,459 --> 00:33:28,749
Half of you will make the cut.

378
00:33:28,839 --> 00:33:30,709
One of you will be named mission leader.

379
00:33:31,469 --> 00:33:33,969
The other half will remain in reserve.

380
00:33:34,969 --> 00:33:36,969
Your instructor is a TOPGUN graduate

381
00:33:37,049 --> 00:33:39,599
with real-world experience
in every mission aspect

382
00:33:39,679 --> 00:33:41,269
you will be expected to master.

383
00:33:42,229 --> 00:33:44,439
His exploits are legendary.

384
00:33:45,899 --> 00:33:48,069
And he's considered
to be one of the finest pilots

385
00:33:48,149 --> 00:33:50,149
this program has ever produced.

386
00:33:51,569 --> 00:33:53,149
What he has to teach you

387
00:33:53,239 --> 00:33:56,619
may very well mean the difference
between life and death.

388
00:33:57,449 --> 00:33:59,789
I give you Captain Pete Mitchell.

389
00:34:00,289 --> 00:34:03,079
"Maverick."

390
00:34:07,629 --> 00:34:08,629
Good morning.

391
00:34:17,009 --> 00:34:18,679
The F-18 NATOPS.

392
00:34:20,259 --> 00:34:23,769
It contains everything they want you
to know about your aircraft.

393
00:34:24,769 --> 00:34:27,559
I'm assuming you know the book
inside and out.

394
00:34:27,649 --> 00:34:28,899
-Damn right.
-Damn straight.

395
00:34:28,979 --> 00:34:30,149
You got it.

396
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:39,699
So does your enemy.

397
00:34:40,279 --> 00:34:41,789
And we're off.

398
00:34:42,829 --> 00:34:46,039
But what the enemy doesn't know
is your limits.

399
00:34:46,829 --> 00:34:48,538
I intend to find them,

400
00:34:48,628 --> 00:34:50,248
test them,

401
00:34:50,838 --> 00:34:52,208
push beyond.

402
00:34:53,378 --> 00:34:56,968
Today we'll start
with what you only think you know.

403
00:34:58,888 --> 00:35:00,678
You show me what you're made of.

404
00:35:05,808 --> 00:35:06,808
Rooster.

405
00:35:07,978 --> 00:35:09,018
Bradley.

406
00:35:09,648 --> 00:35:11,398
Lieutenant Bradshaw!

407
00:35:13,398 --> 00:35:14,398
Yes, sir.

408
00:35:15,398 --> 00:35:17,108
Let's not do it like this.

409
00:35:17,908 --> 00:35:19,278
You gonna wash me out?

410
00:35:20,908 --> 00:35:22,618
That'll be up to you, not me.

411
00:35:24,908 --> 00:35:26,288
Am I dismissed?

412
00:35:43,848 --> 00:35:46,268
Good morning, aviators.
This is your captain speaking.

413
00:35:46,348 --> 00:35:48,478
Welcome to basic fighter maneuvers.

414
00:35:50,018 --> 00:35:52,978
As briefed,
today's exercise is dogfighting.

415
00:35:53,068 --> 00:35:54,688
Guns only, no missiles.

416
00:35:55,688 --> 00:35:58,818
We do not go below the hard deck
of 5,000 feet.

417
00:35:58,898 --> 00:36:01,818
Working as a team,
you have to shoot me down, or else.

418
00:36:01,908 --> 00:36:05,238
-Or else what, sir?
-Or else I shoot back.

419
00:36:05,328 --> 00:36:08,248
If I shoot either one of you down,
you both lose.

420
00:36:08,328 --> 00:36:10,208
This guy needs an ego check.

421
00:36:10,288 --> 00:36:11,628
We'll see to that.

422
00:36:11,708 --> 00:36:14,378
-What say we put some skin in the game?
-What do you have in mind?

423
00:36:14,458 --> 00:36:17,338
Whoever gets shot down first
has to do 200 push-ups.

424
00:36:17,418 --> 00:36:20,178
Guys. That's a lot of push-ups.

425
00:36:20,258 --> 00:36:22,388
They don't call it an exercise
for nothing, sir.

426
00:36:22,468 --> 00:36:24,388
You got yourself a deal, gentlemen.

427
00:36:24,468 --> 00:36:26,768
Fight's on. Let's turn and burn.

428
00:36:28,348 --> 00:36:29,598
Fanboy, you see him?

429
00:36:29,688 --> 00:36:32,688
Nothing on radar up ahead.
He must be somewhere behind us.

430
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:36,938
-Damn it!
-What the hell?

431
00:36:37,028 --> 00:36:37,858
Shit!

432
00:36:42,568 --> 00:36:43,408
Easy, Maverick.

433
00:36:43,488 --> 00:36:46,577
Let's try not to get fired
on the first day.

434
00:36:46,657 --> 00:36:49,577
Tally, tally, tally! Maverick's coming in!
Break left!

435
00:36:49,657 --> 00:36:50,827
Breaking left.

436
00:36:52,827 --> 00:36:54,877
Payback, where's your wingman?

437
00:36:54,957 --> 00:36:57,167
-Rooster, where are you?
-I got your back.

438
00:36:57,247 --> 00:36:59,757
I'm coming. Hang in there. Hang in there.

439
00:36:59,837 --> 00:37:01,177
Hurry up, man! Hurry up!

440
00:37:04,927 --> 00:37:06,887
-Payback, break right.
-Breaking right.

441
00:37:08,267 --> 00:37:11,687
Rooster just saved your life, fellas.
But it's gonna cost him.

442
00:37:11,767 --> 00:37:13,437
Not this time, old man.

443
00:37:16,107 --> 00:37:17,727
Don't let him get to you, Maverick.

444
00:37:24,697 --> 00:37:27,327
Rooster, you're too low! Pull up!
You're hitting the hard deck!

445
00:37:27,407 --> 00:37:29,907
-Altitude. Altitude.
-Oh, shit.

446
00:37:34,327 --> 00:37:35,327
That's a kill.

447
00:37:35,417 --> 00:37:37,787
Down! 109.

448
00:37:38,747 --> 00:37:41,377
Down! 110.

449
00:37:43,297 --> 00:37:45,047
That should be us down there.

450
00:37:45,137 --> 00:37:46,257
But it's not.

451
00:37:47,047 --> 00:37:49,557
And now you know a little something
about Rooster.

452
00:37:51,557 --> 00:37:53,687
Hold that tarmac down till we get back,
brother, all right?

453
00:37:53,767 --> 00:37:55,477
Get in there, boys.

454
00:37:58,607 --> 00:38:00,357
-That's a kill.
-Damn!

455
00:38:01,107 --> 00:38:02,687
-Smoked.
-Damn it.

456
00:38:03,397 --> 00:38:06,027
It was all fun and games in that selfie,
wasn't it? Down!

457
00:38:06,107 --> 00:38:06,947
Say, Phoenix.

458
00:38:07,027 --> 00:38:09,867
How's about we tell everybody
"Bob" stands for something?

459
00:38:09,947 --> 00:38:12,287
-Other than Robert, I mean.
-Don't take the bait, Bob.

460
00:38:12,367 --> 00:38:14,407
Want to know why we call him Hangman?

461
00:38:14,497 --> 00:38:16,747
I got it. "Baby On Board."

462
00:38:19,167 --> 00:38:20,627
Shit!

463
00:38:21,917 --> 00:38:23,837
Greetings, aviators. Fight's on.

464
00:38:24,467 --> 00:38:26,717
All right, Phoenix,
let's take this guy out!

465
00:38:26,797 --> 00:38:27,967
Watch your back, Phoenix.

466
00:38:28,047 --> 00:38:29,927
-Break right!
-Breaking right.

467
00:38:32,347 --> 00:38:33,347
Where's he going?

468
00:38:33,427 --> 00:38:36,517
That's why we call him Hangman.
He'll always hang you out to dry.

469
00:38:37,517 --> 00:38:39,017
Leaving your wingman.

470
00:38:39,107 --> 00:38:40,767
There's a strategy
I haven't seen in a while.

471
00:38:40,857 --> 00:38:43,277
He called you a man, Phoenix.
You gonna take that?

472
00:38:43,357 --> 00:38:44,777
So long as he doesn't call you a man.

473
00:38:44,857 --> 00:38:46,817
Talk to me, Bob. Where's Maverick?

474
00:38:46,907 --> 00:38:48,907
Jesus, his nose is already coming around!

475
00:38:48,987 --> 00:38:50,367
Get him off me, Hangman!

476
00:38:50,447 --> 00:38:54,407
For all you folks at home,
this is how you bury a fossil.

477
00:38:54,497 --> 00:38:57,117
All right, Hangman.
Time to teach you a lesson.

478
00:38:57,207 --> 00:38:59,077
-You're out, Phoenix.
-Son of a bitch!

479
00:39:00,377 --> 00:39:01,377
That's it.

480
00:39:01,457 --> 00:39:03,957
-Let's go, Mav. Let's see what you got.
-Come get me.

481
00:39:06,377 --> 00:39:08,088
Evil be gone. Hangman's coming.

482
00:39:09,298 --> 00:39:11,508
Yeah, you're good. I'll give you that.

483
00:39:18,018 --> 00:39:21,268
Shit.
Phoenix, I can't see him. How close am I?

484
00:39:21,358 --> 00:39:23,728
-Phoenix?
-I'm dead, dickhead.

485
00:39:23,818 --> 00:39:25,688
See you in the afterlife, Bagman.

486
00:39:27,108 --> 00:39:28,698
Where is he? Where is he?

487
00:39:29,408 --> 00:39:30,698
That's a kill.

488
00:39:31,408 --> 00:39:34,998
Seventy-nine. Down. Eighty. Down.

489
00:39:35,078 --> 00:39:36,248
Let's go. Who's next?

490
00:39:37,498 --> 00:39:39,248
-I got you, Omaha.
-Damn it!

491
00:39:42,288 --> 00:39:44,548
-Lights out, Coyote.
-Copy kill.

492
00:39:44,628 --> 00:39:49,088
Down. Fifty-one. Down. Fifty-two.

493
00:39:51,928 --> 00:39:54,928
So, Rooster, mind if I ask you
a personal question?

494
00:39:55,018 --> 00:39:56,308
Would it matter if I did?

495
00:39:56,388 --> 00:39:58,638
What's the story with you and Maverick?

496
00:39:58,728 --> 00:40:01,768
-It seems like he's got you rattled.
-That's none of your business.

497
00:40:01,858 --> 00:40:03,688
Now where the hell is he?

498
00:40:03,768 --> 00:40:05,438
Been here the whole time.

499
00:40:06,528 --> 00:40:08,358
Holy shit.

500
00:40:10,448 --> 00:40:11,618
You see me now?

501
00:40:12,528 --> 00:40:14,328
Come on, let's get it over with.

502
00:40:14,948 --> 00:40:16,368
Fight's on!

503
00:40:18,078 --> 00:40:20,418
What is with these two?

504
00:40:24,958 --> 00:40:28,418
All right, you put us here.
How you gonna get yourself out?

505
00:40:29,008 --> 00:40:31,088
You can bail out anytime.

506
00:40:31,178 --> 00:40:32,508
How low you want to go, Rooster?

507
00:40:32,588 --> 00:40:35,848
I can go as low as you, sir!
And that's saying something.

508
00:40:39,688 --> 00:40:41,688
What's past is past. For both of us.

509
00:40:41,768 --> 00:40:43,608
You'd like to believe that, wouldn't you?

510
00:40:43,688 --> 00:40:46,778
Hard deck is 5,000 feet, fellas.
You are running out of room.

511
00:40:47,778 --> 00:40:48,778
Altitude.

512
00:40:48,858 --> 00:40:50,858
Your strategy
is about to run us into the ground.

513
00:40:50,948 --> 00:40:53,408
-What's your move?
-Altitude. Altitude.

514
00:40:53,488 --> 00:40:54,868
Altitude.

515
00:40:56,658 --> 00:40:59,538
Altitude. Altitude. Altitude.

516
00:40:59,618 --> 00:41:02,038
Altitude. Altitude.

517
00:41:04,078 --> 00:41:06,748
Pull up! Pull up! Pull up! Pull up!

518
00:41:07,458 --> 00:41:08,458
Pull up! Pull up!

519
00:41:11,718 --> 00:41:13,428
You got it. Don't think, just do.

520
00:41:14,598 --> 00:41:17,138
Come on, Rooster, you got him!
Drop down and take the shot!

521
00:41:18,768 --> 00:41:19,678
It's too low.

522
00:41:20,728 --> 00:41:22,438
Too late. You had your chance.

523
00:41:28,568 --> 00:41:31,318
That's a kill. Knock it off.

524
00:41:32,318 --> 00:41:33,448
Damn it!

525
00:41:33,528 --> 00:41:35,408
Same old Rooster.

526
00:41:37,948 --> 00:41:40,288
Go see Hondo about your push-ups.

527
00:41:48,498 --> 00:41:50,008
All right, that's enough.

528
00:41:50,669 --> 00:41:52,759
Rooster. That's enough, man.

529
00:42:07,149 --> 00:42:10,819
Breaking the hard deck, insubordination.
Are you trying to get kicked out?

530
00:42:10,899 --> 00:42:12,359
Don't worry about it.

531
00:42:12,859 --> 00:42:15,359
Look, I'm going on this mission.

532
00:42:16,319 --> 00:42:19,119
But if you get kicked out,
you leave us flying with Hangman.

533
00:42:19,739 --> 00:42:23,369
-Talk to me. What the hell was that?
-He pulled my papers.

534
00:42:23,459 --> 00:42:26,919
-What? Who?
-Maverick.

535
00:42:28,089 --> 00:42:30,629
He pulled my application
to the Naval Academy.

536
00:42:31,709 --> 00:42:33,719
Set me back four years.

537
00:42:36,219 --> 00:42:37,679
Why would he do that?

538
00:42:43,519 --> 00:42:46,059
The hard deck is 5,000 feet
above ground level.

539
00:42:46,139 --> 00:42:48,479
A parameter is set
not just for the safety of our pilots,

540
00:42:48,559 --> 00:42:50,069
but for the safety of their aircraft.

541
00:42:50,149 --> 00:42:54,359
5,000 feet is not just a rule.
It is a law, as immutable as gravity.

542
00:42:54,439 --> 00:42:57,109
The hard deck will be much lower
for the mission, sir.

543
00:42:57,199 --> 00:43:00,329
And it will not change
without my approval!

544
00:43:00,409 --> 00:43:02,329
Especially not in the middle
of an exercise.

545
00:43:02,999 --> 00:43:06,369
And that Cobra maneuver of yours?
That could've got all three of you killed.

546
00:43:06,459 --> 00:43:08,329
I never want to see that shit again.

547
00:43:09,419 --> 00:43:11,669
What exactly do you suppose
you were teaching, Captain?

548
00:43:11,749 --> 00:43:14,169
That as good as they are, sir,
they still have something to learn.

549
00:43:14,259 --> 00:43:16,839
You are talking about the best
fighter pilots on the planet, Captain.

550
00:43:16,929 --> 00:43:18,679
And they've been told that
their entire career,

551
00:43:18,759 --> 00:43:20,639
while they've been dropping bombs
from a high altitude

552
00:43:20,719 --> 00:43:22,469
with little to no dogfighting.

553
00:43:22,559 --> 00:43:25,309
The parameters of this mission call for
something they have never encountered.

554
00:43:25,389 --> 00:43:29,099
Okay, you have less than three weeks
to teach them how to fight as a team

555
00:43:29,939 --> 00:43:31,229
and how to strike the target.

556
00:43:31,319 --> 00:43:33,069
And how to come home.

557
00:43:35,899 --> 00:43:37,909
And how to come home, sir.

558
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:45,249
Every mission has its risks.

559
00:43:46,119 --> 00:43:47,999
These pilots accept that.

560
00:43:48,079 --> 00:43:49,669
I don't, sir.

561
00:43:53,879 --> 00:43:55,209
Every morning, from this day forward,

562
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:58,009
you will brief us on
your instructional plans in writing.

563
00:43:58,089 --> 00:44:01,009
And nothing will change
without my express approval.

564
00:44:01,089 --> 00:44:04,259
-Including the hard deck, sir?
-Especially the hard deck, Captain.

565
00:44:06,349 --> 00:44:07,429
Sir.

566
00:44:08,349 --> 00:44:09,559
What is this?

567
00:44:09,649 --> 00:44:11,309
It's a request to lower
the hard deck, sir,

568
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:13,819
to practice a low-level bombing run
per the mission parameters.

569
00:44:19,909 --> 00:44:22,529
You could learn a thing or two
about timing, Captain.

570
00:44:23,369 --> 00:44:24,329
Yo, Coyote.

571
00:44:25,039 --> 00:44:26,329
Take a look at this.

572
00:44:30,249 --> 00:44:32,959
The man, the legend. There he is.

573
00:44:33,039 --> 00:44:35,050
No, no, no. Next to him.

574
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:38,050
He look familiar to you?

575
00:44:39,970 --> 00:44:41,590
What have we here?

576
00:44:42,390 --> 00:44:44,100
Bradshaw.

577
00:44:45,060 --> 00:44:46,720
As I live and breathe.

578
00:44:49,940 --> 00:44:52,480
Hey, Theo, you got big.

579
00:44:53,310 --> 00:44:54,440
Hey, Mav.

580
00:45:01,530 --> 00:45:02,570
Amelia?

581
00:45:02,660 --> 00:45:04,200
I know. I got big.

582
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:05,530
Yes.

583
00:45:06,620 --> 00:45:07,910
Bar opens at 5:00.

584
00:45:08,750 --> 00:45:10,750
No, I just came by to pay off a debt.

585
00:45:10,830 --> 00:45:12,080
Mom!

586
00:45:16,800 --> 00:45:19,760
-Hey, how's your dad?
-With his wife, in Hawaii.

587
00:45:19,840 --> 00:45:21,220
Mom!

588
00:45:22,180 --> 00:45:24,300
Mav says he owes you money.

589
00:45:25,800 --> 00:45:27,810
-Don't worry about it.
-I insist.

590
00:45:31,020 --> 00:45:34,690
Thank you, Captain.
Consider your tab closed.

591
00:45:35,690 --> 00:45:37,570
Captain? Still?

592
00:45:38,190 --> 00:45:40,320
A highly decorated captain.

593
00:45:40,400 --> 00:45:41,450
Finish up.

594
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:43,320
We have to get the boat to the yard.

595
00:45:43,410 --> 00:45:45,370
-I can't go.
-What do you mean, you can't go?

596
00:45:45,450 --> 00:45:48,790
Test tomorrow. I have to study.
They only told us today.

597
00:45:48,870 --> 00:45:50,830
Well, I can't sail her alone.

598
00:45:50,910 --> 00:45:52,330
Just use the engine.

599
00:45:52,410 --> 00:45:54,580
Why are we taking her to the yard?

600
00:45:55,210 --> 00:45:56,670
To fix the engine.

601
00:45:57,460 --> 00:45:58,460
I can help.

602
00:46:04,720 --> 00:46:07,930
-Little rougher than I was expecting.
-You don't say.

603
00:46:08,640 --> 00:46:11,600
Pull on the backstay.
We'll de-power the sails.

604
00:46:11,680 --> 00:46:12,680
Okay.

605
00:46:13,230 --> 00:46:14,810
What does that mean?

606
00:46:16,230 --> 00:46:18,480
You're supposed to be in the navy!

607
00:46:18,570 --> 00:46:21,900
I don't sail boats, Penny. I land on them.

608
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:25,660
It's sort of like raising the flaps
on an airplane.

609
00:46:25,740 --> 00:46:27,200
So how do I do that?

610
00:46:27,950 --> 00:46:30,160
You pull on that green line up there.

611
00:46:30,240 --> 00:46:31,580
Green line.

612
00:46:34,120 --> 00:46:35,670
Yep. Pull it hard.

613
00:46:35,750 --> 00:46:38,670
Yep. Crank that winch right there,

614
00:46:38,750 --> 00:46:40,550
tighten the jib.

615
00:46:41,260 --> 00:46:43,590
-Crank it. You okay?
-Yeah.

616
00:46:45,130 --> 00:46:46,090
Good.

617
00:46:47,340 --> 00:46:48,350
Now,

618
00:46:49,760 --> 00:46:51,180
you ready?

619
00:46:53,100 --> 00:46:54,180
For what?

620
00:46:54,770 --> 00:46:56,310
The afterburner.

621
00:47:16,620 --> 00:47:18,460
Now you're in the navy.

622
00:47:40,730 --> 00:47:42,570
Thanks for helping out today.

623
00:47:44,280 --> 00:47:45,690
I'm not exactly sure I helped.

624
00:47:51,160 --> 00:47:52,660
Don't give me that look.

625
00:47:52,740 --> 00:47:54,080
What look?

626
00:47:54,160 --> 00:47:55,790
That one.

627
00:47:59,080 --> 00:48:00,380
Good night, Pete.

628
00:48:01,170 --> 00:48:02,500
Night, Penny.

629
00:48:17,980 --> 00:48:19,480
Mom, is that you?

630
00:48:20,100 --> 00:48:21,400
Yeah, it's me.

631
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:24,110
I'll make you dinner.

632
00:48:24,190 --> 00:48:25,190
Okay.

633
00:48:31,410 --> 00:48:33,660
Time is your greatest enemy.

634
00:48:35,080 --> 00:48:37,200
Phase one of the mission
will be a low-level ingress

635
00:48:37,290 --> 00:48:39,040
attacking in two-plane teams.

636
00:48:39,620 --> 00:48:41,830
You'll fly along this narrow canyon
to your target.

637
00:48:41,920 --> 00:48:45,340
Radar-guided surface-to-air missiles
defend the area.

638
00:48:45,420 --> 00:48:47,670
These SAMs, they're lethal.

639
00:48:48,340 --> 00:48:52,220
But they were designed to protect
the skies above, not the canyon below.

640
00:48:52,300 --> 00:48:56,180
That's because the enemy knows no one is
insane enough to try and fly below them.

641
00:48:57,100 --> 00:48:59,060
That's exactly
what I'm gonna train you to do.

642
00:49:00,100 --> 00:49:04,310
On the day, your altitude
will be 100 feet maximum.

643
00:49:04,400 --> 00:49:07,530
You exceed this altitude,
radar will spot you,

644
00:49:08,400 --> 00:49:09,900
and you're dead.

645
00:49:11,030 --> 00:49:12,990
Your airspeed will be 660 knots

646
00:49:13,820 --> 00:49:15,080
minimum.

647
00:49:15,160 --> 00:49:17,490
Two and a half minutes.

648
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:21,830
That's because fifth-generation fighters
wait at an air base nearby.

649
00:49:22,710 --> 00:49:27,130
In a head-to-head with these planes
in your F-18s, you're dead.

650
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:30,840
That's why you need to get in,
hit your target and be gone

651
00:49:30,920 --> 00:49:34,090
before these planes
even have a chance of catching you.

652
00:49:34,180 --> 00:49:37,010
This makes time your greatest adversary.

653
00:49:38,850 --> 00:49:42,140
You'll fly a route in your nav system
that simulates the canyon.

654
00:49:42,940 --> 00:49:44,610
The faster you navigate this canyon,

655
00:49:44,690 --> 00:49:47,360
the harder it'll be to stay
under the radar of these enemy SAMs.

656
00:49:48,360 --> 00:49:49,480
The tighter the turns,

657
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:52,780
the more intensely the force of gravity
on your body multiplies,

658
00:49:53,450 --> 00:49:55,200
compressing your lungs,

659
00:49:55,280 --> 00:49:56,700
forcing the blood from your brain,

660
00:49:56,780 --> 00:50:00,000
impairing your judgment and reaction time.

661
00:50:00,080 --> 00:50:02,460
So for today's lesson,
we're gonna take it easy on you.

662
00:50:02,540 --> 00:50:05,540
- 300 feet.
- Three minutes.

663
00:50:07,420 --> 00:50:08,630
Good luck.

664
00:50:17,050 --> 00:50:18,850
Time to target is one minute 30.

665
00:50:18,930 --> 00:50:21,350
We are two seconds behind.
Increase to 480 knots.

666
00:50:21,430 --> 00:50:22,680
We got to move, Coyote.

667
00:50:23,560 --> 00:50:25,230
Copy. Increasing speed.

668
00:50:27,610 --> 00:50:28,520
Oh, shit!

669
00:50:32,320 --> 00:50:33,360
Why are they dead?

670
00:50:33,450 --> 00:50:36,240
We broke the 300-foot ceiling,
and a SAM took us out.

671
00:50:36,320 --> 00:50:37,950
No. Why are they dead?

672
00:50:38,030 --> 00:50:40,370
I slowed down and didn't give her
a warning. It was my fault.

673
00:50:40,450 --> 00:50:42,290
Was there a reason
you didn't communicate with your team?

674
00:50:42,370 --> 00:50:43,500
I was focusing on--

675
00:50:43,580 --> 00:50:45,370
One that their family will accept
at the funeral.

676
00:50:46,380 --> 00:50:47,330
None, sir.

677
00:50:48,290 --> 00:50:51,340
Why didn't you anticipate the turn?
You were briefed on the terrain.

678
00:50:51,960 --> 00:50:54,680
Don't tell me. Tell it to his family.

679
00:51:00,100 --> 00:51:02,640
Hangman, ease up.
The canyon's getting tighter.

680
00:51:02,720 --> 00:51:05,310
Negative, Payback. Increase your speed.

681
00:51:06,940 --> 00:51:10,270
-You're going too fast, man.
-No harm in being ahead of schedule.

682
00:51:12,480 --> 00:51:15,450
Damn it, slow down!
I can't stay on the course!

683
00:51:15,530 --> 00:51:18,120
You're gonna hit the wall!
Watch out! Watch out!

684
00:51:21,830 --> 00:51:24,540
-What happened?
-I flew as fast as I could.

685
00:51:25,120 --> 00:51:26,710
Kind of like my ass depended on it.

686
00:51:26,790 --> 00:51:30,000
And you put your team in danger,
and your wingman's dead.

687
00:51:31,210 --> 00:51:32,750
They couldn't keep up.

688
00:51:38,890 --> 00:51:41,510
Rooster,
we're 20 seconds behind and dropping.

689
00:51:41,600 --> 00:51:44,180
We're fine. Speed is good.

690
00:51:44,270 --> 00:51:45,810
Increase to 500 knots.

691
00:51:45,890 --> 00:51:48,940
-Negative, Yale. Hold your speed.
-Rooster, we're late!

692
00:51:49,020 --> 00:51:51,820
We're alive.
We'll make up time in the straightaway.

693
00:51:51,900 --> 00:51:53,480
We are not gonna make it.

694
00:51:53,570 --> 00:51:56,570
Just trust me. Maintain your speed.
We can make it.

695
00:51:56,650 --> 00:51:57,780
Why are you dead?

696
00:51:59,110 --> 00:52:03,080
You're team leader up there.
Why are you, why is your team dead?

697
00:52:03,160 --> 00:52:05,830
Sir, he's the only one
who made it to the target.

698
00:52:05,910 --> 00:52:07,120
A minute late.

699
00:52:07,920 --> 00:52:10,500
He gave enemy aircraft time
to shoot him down.

700
00:52:10,580 --> 00:52:12,420
-He is dead.
-You don't know that.

701
00:52:12,500 --> 00:52:16,010
You're not flying fast enough.
You don't have a second to waste.

702
00:52:16,090 --> 00:52:17,340
We made it to the target.

703
00:52:17,420 --> 00:52:21,140
And superior enemy aircraft
intercepted you on your way out.

704
00:52:21,220 --> 00:52:24,220
-Then it's a dogfight.
-Against fifth-generation fighters.

705
00:52:24,310 --> 00:52:26,890
-Yeah. We'd still have a chance.
-In an F-18.

706
00:52:26,980 --> 00:52:29,480
It's not the plane, sir, it's the pilot.

707
00:52:29,560 --> 00:52:30,690
Exactly!

708
00:52:37,820 --> 00:52:40,490
There's more than one way
to fly this mission.

709
00:52:40,570 --> 00:52:42,530
You really don't get it.

710
00:52:43,530 --> 00:52:46,200
On this mission,
a man flies like Maverick here,

711
00:52:46,290 --> 00:52:48,120
or a man does not come back.

712
00:52:49,120 --> 00:52:51,210
No offense intended.

713
00:52:51,290 --> 00:52:53,590
Yet somehow you always manage.

714
00:52:55,130 --> 00:52:57,920
Look, I don't mean to criticize.
You're conservative, that's all.

715
00:52:58,010 --> 00:52:58,840
Lieutenant.

716
00:52:58,920 --> 00:53:03,510
We're going into combat, son,
on a level no living pilot's ever seen.

717
00:53:05,060 --> 00:53:06,180
Not even him.

718
00:53:08,180 --> 00:53:10,020
That's no time to be thinking
about the past.

719
00:53:14,110 --> 00:53:16,150
-What's that supposed to mean?
-Rooster.

720
00:53:16,230 --> 00:53:18,820
I can't be the only one that knows
that Maverick flew with his old man.

721
00:53:18,900 --> 00:53:20,360
-That's enough.
-Or that Maverick was flying

722
00:53:20,450 --> 00:53:22,160
-when his old man--
-Lieutenant, that's enough!

723
00:53:24,120 --> 00:53:25,990
-That's enough.
-You son of a bitch!

724
00:53:26,080 --> 00:53:27,040
Hey, come on!

725
00:53:27,120 --> 00:53:29,620
I'm cool, I'm cool. Hey, hey, hey.

726
00:53:29,710 --> 00:53:30,540
That's enough.

727
00:53:30,620 --> 00:53:32,710
-He's not cut out for this mission.
-That's enough!

728
00:53:32,790 --> 00:53:34,040
You know it.

729
00:53:37,090 --> 00:53:38,090
You know I'm right.

730
00:53:44,550 --> 00:53:45,680
You're all dismissed.

731
00:54:49,990 --> 00:54:51,370
Maverick.

732
00:54:53,710 --> 00:54:55,000
It's come back?

733
00:54:55,670 --> 00:54:57,130
No one knows.

734
00:54:59,290 --> 00:55:01,000
There's nothing else they can do.

735
00:55:01,880 --> 00:55:04,880
Even speaking is painful now.

736
00:55:10,890 --> 00:55:12,600
Sarah, I'm so sorry.

737
00:55:32,290 --> 00:55:33,290
Admiral.

738
00:55:44,840 --> 00:55:46,050
How's my wingman?

739
00:55:57,690 --> 00:55:59,980
Please, don't worry about me.

740
00:56:00,940 --> 00:56:02,690
What can I do for you?

741
00:56:11,160 --> 00:56:12,240
All right.

742
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:18,210
Well, Rooster's still angry with me
about what I did.

743
00:56:19,710 --> 00:56:22,460
I thought eventually
he would understand why.

744
00:56:24,710 --> 00:56:26,380
I hoped he'd forgive me.

745
00:56:34,810 --> 00:56:36,730
The mission is less than three weeks away.

746
00:56:37,310 --> 00:56:38,890
The kid's not ready.

747
00:56:47,240 --> 00:56:49,200
He doesn't want what I have to give.

748
00:56:50,410 --> 00:56:51,660
Ice, please,

749
00:56:51,740 --> 00:56:54,080
don't ask me to send someone else to die.

750
00:56:54,160 --> 00:56:55,290
Please don't...

751
00:56:56,290 --> 00:56:57,870
Don't ask me to send him.

752
00:56:57,960 --> 00:56:59,540
Send me.

753
00:57:31,320 --> 00:57:32,990
I don't know how.

754
00:57:46,210 --> 00:57:47,960
I'm not a teacher, Ice.

755
00:57:50,380 --> 00:57:52,220
I'm a fighter pilot.

756
00:57:54,800 --> 00:57:56,220
A naval aviator.

757
00:57:58,720 --> 00:58:00,810
It's not what I am.

758
00:58:02,060 --> 00:58:03,650
It's who I am.

759
00:58:05,400 --> 00:58:07,150
How do I teach that?

760
00:58:09,030 --> 00:58:11,650
Even if I could teach it,
it's not what Rooster wants.

761
00:58:12,610 --> 00:58:14,780
It's not what the navy wants.

762
00:58:14,870 --> 00:58:17,200
That's why they canned me the last time.

763
00:58:20,040 --> 00:58:23,000
The only reason I'm here is you.

764
00:58:30,340 --> 00:58:32,170
If I send him on this mission,

765
00:58:33,590 --> 00:58:35,470
he might never come home.

766
00:58:39,220 --> 00:58:40,850
And if I don't send him,

767
00:58:41,560 --> 00:58:43,390
he'll never forgive me.

768
00:58:46,100 --> 00:58:48,570
Either way, I could lose him forever.

769
00:58:59,029 --> 00:59:00,039
I know.

770
00:59:00,869 --> 00:59:02,199
I know.

771
00:59:13,379 --> 00:59:17,009
The navy needs Maverick.

772
00:59:19,049 --> 00:59:22,599
The kid needs Maverick.

773
00:59:23,679 --> 00:59:25,939
That's why I fought for you.

774
00:59:27,939 --> 00:59:30,269
That's why you're still here.

775
00:59:38,319 --> 00:59:40,079
Thank you, Ice,

776
00:59:40,739 --> 00:59:42,159
for everything.

777
00:59:47,079 --> 00:59:48,539
One last thing.

778
00:59:49,169 --> 00:59:50,919
Who's the better pilot?

779
00:59:50,999 --> 00:59:52,299
You or me?

780
00:59:55,419 --> 00:59:58,009
This is a nice moment. Let's not ruin it.

781
01:00:38,379 --> 01:00:40,089
All right, all right.

782
01:02:01,679 --> 01:02:02,679
Sir.

783
01:02:02,759 --> 01:02:04,799
-What is this?
-This is dogfight football.

784
01:02:04,889 --> 01:02:07,059
Offense and defense at the same time.

785
01:02:07,889 --> 01:02:08,889
Who's winning?

786
01:02:08,969 --> 01:02:11,889
I think they stopped keeping score
a while ago.

787
01:02:11,979 --> 01:02:15,019
This detachment still has some training
to complete, Captain.

788
01:02:15,109 --> 01:02:17,319
-Every available minute matters.
-Yes, sir.

789
01:02:17,399 --> 01:02:19,609
So why are we out here playing games?

790
01:02:19,689 --> 01:02:21,569
You said to create a team, sir.

791
01:02:23,069 --> 01:02:24,619
There's your team.

792
01:04:04,008 --> 01:04:06,588
Should I go? Before Amelia gets back?

793
01:04:06,678 --> 01:04:09,008
-She'll be at her friend's house tonight.
-Oh, good.

794
01:04:12,178 --> 01:04:13,848
You and Amelia, you seem...

795
01:04:16,598 --> 01:04:19,018
a lot closer than when I last saw you.

796
01:04:19,098 --> 01:04:21,518
-Yeah. Yeah, we are.
-How do you manage?

797
01:04:23,688 --> 01:04:24,818
Well,

798
01:04:26,488 --> 01:04:29,698
you know, she always wanted more freedom
than I thought she was ready for.

799
01:04:30,448 --> 01:04:32,408
Where'd she get that from, I wonder?

800
01:04:36,038 --> 01:04:37,458
I guess I realized

801
01:04:38,368 --> 01:04:40,458
I also had to trust her.

802
01:04:42,038 --> 01:04:44,548
Let her make some
of her own mistakes sometimes.

803
01:04:47,048 --> 01:04:48,718
Not an easy choice.

804
01:04:53,058 --> 01:04:55,058
Is that what happened with Rooster?

805
01:04:58,728 --> 01:05:01,478
I pulled his papers
from the Naval Academy.

806
01:05:04,528 --> 01:05:06,238
Took years off his career.

807
01:05:12,529 --> 01:05:13,529
Why?

808
01:05:16,449 --> 01:05:19,959
His mother never wanted him to fly,
not after what happened to Goose.

809
01:05:22,749 --> 01:05:26,169
She made me promise before she died, so...

810
01:05:26,259 --> 01:05:28,169
Does Rooster know that?

811
01:05:31,719 --> 01:05:34,759
He will always resent me for what I did.

812
01:05:36,769 --> 01:05:38,769
Why should he resent her too?

813
01:05:43,689 --> 01:05:45,399
Not an easy choice.

814
01:05:48,359 --> 01:05:50,859
I was trying to be the father he lost.

815
01:05:53,949 --> 01:05:54,949
I just--

816
01:05:57,829 --> 01:05:59,999
I wish I would've done it better.

817
01:06:02,249 --> 01:06:05,089
But the truth is...

818
01:06:07,629 --> 01:06:09,459
I didn't think he was ready.

819
01:06:13,049 --> 01:06:14,759
Is he ready now?

820
01:06:18,219 --> 01:06:19,639
Mom, I'm home!

821
01:06:21,390 --> 01:06:23,810
I thought you were staying
at Karen's tonight.

822
01:06:23,900 --> 01:06:26,650
Karen's sick. And I've got homework to do.

823
01:06:26,730 --> 01:06:29,150
-I should go.
-You should go.

824
01:06:29,740 --> 01:06:32,530
-Have you had dinner yet?
-Not yet. You want to go out?

825
01:06:32,610 --> 01:06:35,570
No, it's okay. I'll make you something.

826
01:06:35,660 --> 01:06:36,740
I'll be down in a sec!

827
01:06:37,620 --> 01:06:39,580
-Wait! Not that way.
-What?

828
01:06:41,250 --> 01:06:43,460
Look, I have an example to set.

829
01:06:43,540 --> 01:06:46,000
I can't be bringing guys home
on a first date.

830
01:06:46,080 --> 01:06:47,420
This is not our first date.

831
01:06:48,590 --> 01:06:50,130
You know what I mean.

832
01:06:52,880 --> 01:06:53,880
Okay.

833
01:06:55,050 --> 01:06:56,090
Fine.

834
01:06:57,140 --> 01:06:59,430
But this is the last time
I go out your window.

835
01:06:59,520 --> 01:07:00,970
We'll see.

836
01:07:01,060 --> 01:07:02,480
No. No, I mean it.

837
01:07:03,230 --> 01:07:05,150
I'm never gonna leave you again.

838
01:07:07,150 --> 01:07:08,770
Oh, shut up.

839
01:07:08,860 --> 01:07:10,730
Go on, get out of here.

840
01:07:24,290 --> 01:07:26,250
Just don't break her heart again.

841
01:07:38,221 --> 01:07:39,221
Good morning.

842
01:07:39,301 --> 01:07:41,431
The uranium enrichment plant
that is your target

843
01:07:41,521 --> 01:07:43,981
will be operational earlier than expected.

844
01:07:44,061 --> 01:07:47,191
Raw uranium will be delivered
to the plant in ten days' time.

845
01:07:47,901 --> 01:07:50,981
As a result, your mission
has been moved up one week

846
01:07:51,071 --> 01:07:54,701
in order to avoid contaminating
the target valley with radiation.

847
01:07:54,781 --> 01:07:57,611
Sir, no one here has successfully flown
a low-level course.

848
01:07:57,701 --> 01:07:59,621
Nevertheless,
you've been ordered to move on.

849
01:08:00,831 --> 01:08:01,831
Captain.

850
01:08:04,871 --> 01:08:07,251
We have one week left
to focus on phase two.

851
01:08:07,331 --> 01:08:09,211
It's the most difficult stage
of the mission.

852
01:08:09,291 --> 01:08:11,091
It's a pop-up strike with a steep dive,

853
01:08:11,171 --> 01:08:14,091
requiring nothing less
than two consecutive miracles.

854
01:08:15,261 --> 01:08:18,431
Two pairs of F-18s will fly
in a welded wing formation.

855
01:08:18,511 --> 01:08:19,761
Teamwork.

856
01:08:19,851 --> 01:08:22,351
Precise coordination of these aircraft
is essential

857
01:08:22,431 --> 01:08:25,141
to both the mission's success
and your survival.

858
01:08:25,221 --> 01:08:27,941
As you know,
the plant rests between two mountains.

859
01:08:28,061 --> 01:08:32,111
On final approach,
you'll invert directly into a steep dive.

860
01:08:33,111 --> 01:08:35,782
This allows you to maintain
the lowest possible altitude

861
01:08:36,992 --> 01:08:38,782
and the only possible attack angle.

862
01:08:42,532 --> 01:08:46,372
Your target is an impact point
less than three meters wide.

863
01:08:47,622 --> 01:08:50,542
The two-seat aircraft will paint
the target with a laser bull's-eye.

864
01:08:52,002 --> 01:08:53,882
The first pair will breach the reactor

865
01:08:53,962 --> 01:08:57,632
by dropping a laser-guided bomb
on an exposed ventilation hatch.

866
01:08:57,722 --> 01:08:59,932
This will create an opening
for the second pair.

867
01:09:00,762 --> 01:09:02,222
That's miracle number one.

868
01:09:04,522 --> 01:09:05,972
The second team

869
01:09:06,062 --> 01:09:07,392
will deliver the kill shot

870
01:09:08,732 --> 01:09:10,522
and destroy the target.

871
01:09:11,772 --> 01:09:13,112
That's miracle number two.

872
01:09:14,482 --> 01:09:16,742
If either team misses the target...

873
01:09:19,032 --> 01:09:19,912
That's a miss.

874
01:09:19,992 --> 01:09:21,992
-...the mission is a failure.
-Damn it!

875
01:09:22,702 --> 01:09:26,502
Egress is a steep high-G climb out
to avoid hitting this mountain.

876
01:09:29,372 --> 01:09:32,673
A steep climb at that speed,
you're pulling at least eight G's.

877
01:09:32,753 --> 01:09:34,253
Nine, minimum.

878
01:09:34,343 --> 01:09:37,133
The stress limit
of the F-18's airframe is 7.5.

879
01:09:37,213 --> 01:09:38,593
That's the accepted limit.

880
01:09:38,673 --> 01:09:40,883
To survive this mission,
you'll pull beyond that,

881
01:09:40,973 --> 01:09:43,643
even if it means bending your airframe.

882
01:09:44,973 --> 01:09:48,353
You'll be pulling so hard,
you'll weigh close to 2,000 pounds,

883
01:09:48,433 --> 01:09:51,313
your skull crushing your spine,

884
01:09:51,443 --> 01:09:54,483
your lungs imploding
like an elephant's sitting on your chest,

885
01:09:54,573 --> 01:09:57,993
fighting with everything you have
just to keep from blacking out.

886
01:10:00,073 --> 01:10:02,573
And this is where you'll be
at your most vulnerable.

887
01:10:03,533 --> 01:10:06,413
This is Coffin Corner.

888
01:10:06,493 --> 01:10:09,253
Assuming you avoid crashing
into this mountain,

889
01:10:09,333 --> 01:10:12,923
you'll climb straight up into enemy radar
while losing all of your airspeed.

890
01:10:13,503 --> 01:10:16,133
Within seconds,
you'll be fired upon by enemy SAMs.

891
01:10:17,633 --> 01:10:19,843
You've all faced sustained G's before,
but this--

892
01:10:20,593 --> 01:10:24,263
this is gonna take you and your aircraft
to the breaking point.

893
01:10:24,343 --> 01:10:27,104
Sir, is this even achievable?

894
01:10:27,184 --> 01:10:28,854
The answer to that question

895
01:10:29,434 --> 01:10:31,444
will come down to the pilot in the box.

896
01:10:41,364 --> 01:10:43,614
-Talk to me, Bob.
-We are 12 seconds late on target.

897
01:10:43,704 --> 01:10:46,414
-We got to move! We got to move!
-Copy. Try to stay with me.

898
01:10:50,414 --> 01:10:51,624
Wait, who's that?

899
01:10:52,924 --> 01:10:54,294
Blue Team, you've been spotted.

900
01:10:54,374 --> 01:10:57,004
-Shit, it's Maverick.
-What the hell is he doing here?

901
01:10:57,094 --> 01:11:00,214
I'm a bandit on course to intercept.
Blue Team, what are you gonna do?

902
01:11:00,304 --> 01:11:03,514
He's 20 miles left. Ten o'clock.
700 knots closure.

903
01:11:03,594 --> 01:11:05,434
Your call. What do you want to do?

904
01:11:05,514 --> 01:11:08,224
Continue. We're close. Stay on target.

905
01:11:08,314 --> 01:11:11,523
-He's swinging around to the north!
-Stand by for pop-up.

906
01:11:11,603 --> 01:11:13,693
-Be ready on that laser, Bob.
-Copy. I'm on it.

907
01:11:15,943 --> 01:11:17,653
Blue Team, bandit is still closing.

908
01:11:17,733 --> 01:11:18,903
Popping now.

909
01:11:25,073 --> 01:11:27,203
Talk to me, Bob. Where's Maverick?

910
01:11:27,283 --> 01:11:29,333
He's five miles out. He's coming fast.

911
01:11:35,213 --> 01:11:37,713
-Target's in sight.
-Where's my laser, Bob?

912
01:11:38,543 --> 01:11:41,922
Deadeye! Deadeye! It's no good.
Sorry, I can't get a lock.

913
01:11:42,012 --> 01:11:43,842
We're out of time. I'm dropping blind.

914
01:11:47,092 --> 01:11:48,512
Damn it, missed!

915
01:12:00,112 --> 01:12:02,282
-That's tone.
-Maverick's got missile lock on us.

916
01:12:02,362 --> 01:12:03,402
Shit! We're dead.

917
01:12:04,242 --> 01:12:06,992
Blue Team, that's a fail.
Level out, Coyote.

918
01:12:09,662 --> 01:12:11,581
Coyote? Do you copy?

919
01:12:14,411 --> 01:12:15,871
Coyote, come in.

920
01:12:16,501 --> 01:12:18,421
Coyote, level wings.

921
01:12:18,501 --> 01:12:20,091
Oh, God. He's in G-LOC.

922
01:12:20,841 --> 01:12:23,381
Coyote? Coyote?

923
01:12:23,461 --> 01:12:25,671
-He's gonna burn in!
-I'm going after him.

924
01:12:29,391 --> 01:12:31,681
Come on.
Give me tone, give me tone, give me tone.

925
01:12:32,221 --> 01:12:34,641
Snap out of it, Coyote. Come on! Come on!

926
01:12:37,691 --> 01:12:40,441
Come on, Coyote, come on. Come on!

927
01:12:40,521 --> 01:12:42,690
-Damn it! Coyote!
-Pull up!

928
01:12:42,770 --> 01:12:45,400
-Coyote! Coyote!
-Pull up! Pull up!

929
01:12:50,620 --> 01:12:52,410
Coyote, you okay?

930
01:12:53,450 --> 01:12:55,200
I'm okay. I'm good.

931
01:12:56,210 --> 01:12:59,040
Good. Good. That's enough for today.

932
01:13:01,250 --> 01:13:02,460
That was close.

933
01:13:03,050 --> 01:13:03,960
Too close.

934
01:13:04,840 --> 01:13:07,010
Bird strike! Bird strike!

935
01:13:07,090 --> 01:13:08,220
Bird strike!

936
01:13:11,549 --> 01:13:14,219
-Phoenix, left engine's on fire!
-Climbing.

937
01:13:16,229 --> 01:13:18,729
Throttling back.
Shutting off fuel to left engine.

938
01:13:18,809 --> 01:13:20,439
Extinguishing fire.

939
01:13:22,809 --> 01:13:23,819
Right engine is out!

940
01:13:23,899 --> 01:13:25,569
It's still spinning. Trying to restart it.

941
01:13:28,069 --> 01:13:30,699
-Phoenix, it's on fire. Don't start it.
-Throttling up.

942
01:13:32,279 --> 01:13:33,529
Oh, my God.

943
01:13:36,909 --> 01:13:39,329
-We're on fire! We're on fire!
-Damn it!

944
01:13:39,409 --> 01:13:42,168
-Engine fire. Right.
-Extinguishing right engine.

945
01:13:45,458 --> 01:13:47,378
Phoenix, Bob, punch out, punch out!

946
01:13:47,458 --> 01:13:49,678
Warning lights everywhere!
Hydraulic failure!

947
01:13:49,758 --> 01:13:51,468
-Flight controls.
-I can't control it.

948
01:13:51,548 --> 01:13:54,298
We're going down, Phoenix!
We're going in! We're going in!

949
01:13:54,388 --> 01:13:57,018
You can't save it. Eject, eject!

950
01:13:57,098 --> 01:13:58,268
Eject, eject, eject!

951
01:13:58,348 --> 01:14:01,188
Altitude. Altitude.

952
01:14:22,708 --> 01:14:25,708
They'll keep Phoenix and Bob
in the hospital overnight for observation.

953
01:14:25,788 --> 01:14:27,298
They're gonna be okay.

954
01:14:31,378 --> 01:14:32,718
That's good.

955
01:14:35,968 --> 01:14:37,808
I've never lost a wingman.

956
01:14:38,558 --> 01:14:39,768
You're lucky.

957
01:14:40,348 --> 01:14:42,188
Fly long enough, it'll happen.

958
01:14:44,978 --> 01:14:46,648
There will be others.

959
01:14:49,398 --> 01:14:51,398
Easy for you to say. No wife.

960
01:14:53,358 --> 01:14:54,568
No kids.

961
01:14:55,408 --> 01:14:57,908
Nobody to mourn you when you burn in.

962
01:15:01,158 --> 01:15:02,498
Go home.

963
01:15:03,618 --> 01:15:05,078
Just get some sleep.

964
01:15:07,628 --> 01:15:09,838
Why'd you pull my papers at the Academy?

965
01:15:09,918 --> 01:15:11,548
Why did you stand in my way?

966
01:15:14,128 --> 01:15:15,468
You weren't ready.

967
01:15:15,548 --> 01:15:16,848
Ready for what?

968
01:15:18,508 --> 01:15:20,308
-Ready to fly like you?
-No.

969
01:15:20,388 --> 01:15:22,018
Ready to forget the book.

970
01:15:22,098 --> 01:15:24,808
Trust your instincts.
Don't think, just do.

971
01:15:24,898 --> 01:15:27,558
You think up there, you're dead.
Believe me.

972
01:15:28,858 --> 01:15:30,528
My dad believed in you.

973
01:15:33,238 --> 01:15:35,698
I'm not gonna make the same mistake.

974
01:15:41,368 --> 01:15:42,868
Maverick.

975
01:15:53,418 --> 01:15:56,298
Ready, aim, fire.

976
01:16:01,058 --> 01:16:02,217
Ready,

977
01:16:02,717 --> 01:16:03,767
aim,

978
01:16:04,307 --> 01:16:05,637
fire.

979
01:16:15,697 --> 01:16:16,907
Ready,

980
01:16:17,947 --> 01:16:19,317
aim,

981
01:16:19,407 --> 01:16:20,697
fire.

982
01:16:54,477 --> 01:16:56,647
I can only imagine
what you must be feeling right now.

983
01:16:57,737 --> 01:16:59,987
Take some time. Whatever you need.

984
01:17:01,447 --> 01:17:03,617
I appreciate that, sir,
but there is no time. The mission--

985
01:17:03,697 --> 01:17:05,787
I'll be taking over the training
from here.

986
01:17:06,787 --> 01:17:07,787
Sir?

987
01:17:09,207 --> 01:17:10,997
We both know you didn't want this job,
Captain.

988
01:17:11,077 --> 01:17:13,417
-Sir, they're not ready.
-It was your job to get them ready.

989
01:17:13,497 --> 01:17:16,967
Sir, they have to believe
that this mission can be flown.

990
01:17:17,047 --> 01:17:19,797
And all you've managed to do
is teach them that it can't.

991
01:17:20,637 --> 01:17:22,967
-Sir--
-You're grounded, Captain.

992
01:17:23,057 --> 01:17:24,557
Permanently.

993
01:17:28,437 --> 01:17:29,727
-Sir--
-That is all.

994
01:17:48,247 --> 01:17:49,247
I heard.

995
01:17:51,537 --> 01:17:52,707
I'm sorry.

996
01:17:53,587 --> 01:17:55,247
What are you gonna do?

997
01:17:56,417 --> 01:17:57,707
Ice is gone.

998
01:18:00,257 --> 01:18:01,967
What choice do I have?

999
01:18:03,177 --> 01:18:05,757
You'll have to find a way back
on your own.

1000
01:18:05,847 --> 01:18:07,097
No, Penny.

1001
01:18:08,887 --> 01:18:10,227
I'm out.

1002
01:18:11,977 --> 01:18:13,227
This is over.

1003
01:18:13,767 --> 01:18:14,767
Pete.

1004
01:18:14,857 --> 01:18:17,317
If you lost your wingman up there,

1005
01:18:18,067 --> 01:18:19,777
you'd keep fighting.

1006
01:18:19,857 --> 01:18:21,147
You wouldn't just give up.

1007
01:18:21,947 --> 01:18:23,907
Those are your pilots.

1008
01:18:25,197 --> 01:18:27,367
If anything happens to them,

1009
01:18:28,197 --> 01:18:30,247
you'll never forgive yourself.

1010
01:18:34,287 --> 01:18:36,167
I don't know what to do.

1011
01:18:40,217 --> 01:18:41,757
But you'll find a way.

1012
01:18:44,177 --> 01:18:45,387
I know you will.

1013
01:18:47,557 --> 01:18:49,927
Captain Mitchell
is no longer your instructor.

1014
01:18:50,017 --> 01:18:52,437
And as of today,
there are new mission parameters.

1015
01:18:53,187 --> 01:18:55,057
Time to target is now four minutes.

1016
01:18:55,807 --> 01:18:58,357
You'll be entering the valley level
at reduced speed.

1017
01:18:58,437 --> 01:19:01,397
Not to exceed 420 knots.

1018
01:19:01,487 --> 01:19:04,277
Sir, won't we be giving their planes
time to intercept?

1019
01:19:04,357 --> 01:19:06,867
Well, Lieutenant, you have
a fighting chance against enemy aircraft.

1020
01:19:06,947 --> 01:19:10,037
What are the odds of surviving
a head-on collision with a mountain?

1021
01:19:10,117 --> 01:19:12,707
You'll be attacking the target
from a higher altitude,

1022
01:19:12,787 --> 01:19:13,997
level with the north wall.

1023
01:19:14,077 --> 01:19:16,497
Gonna be a little harder
to keep your lase on target,

1024
01:19:16,587 --> 01:19:18,497
but you will avoid the high-G climb out.

1025
01:19:18,587 --> 01:19:20,797
We'll be sitting ducks for enemy missiles.

1026
01:19:26,217 --> 01:19:27,467
Who the hell is that?

1027
01:19:29,257 --> 01:19:32,097
Maverick to Range Control.
Entering Point Alpha.

1028
01:19:32,177 --> 01:19:33,847
Confirm green range.

1029
01:19:34,477 --> 01:19:36,807
Maverick, Range Control,

1030
01:19:36,897 --> 01:19:38,517
green range is confirmed.

1031
01:19:38,607 --> 01:19:41,987
I don't see an event scheduled
for you, sir.

1032
01:19:42,067 --> 01:19:43,277
Well, I'm going anyway.

1033
01:19:43,947 --> 01:19:45,197
Nice.

1034
01:19:45,947 --> 01:19:48,987
Two minutes 15 seconds.

1035
01:19:49,077 --> 01:19:50,827
2:15? That's impossible.

1036
01:19:50,907 --> 01:19:53,457
Final attack point. Maverick's inbound.

1037
01:21:31,137 --> 01:21:34,347
Popping in three, two, one.

1038
01:22:00,827 --> 01:22:02,207
Bombs away.

1039
01:22:19,687 --> 01:22:21,597
Bull's-eye! Holy shit!

1040
01:22:22,897 --> 01:22:24,477
Yes.

1041
01:22:27,357 --> 01:22:28,487
Damn.

1042
01:22:41,247 --> 01:22:43,457
You have put me
in a difficult position, Captain.

1043
01:22:44,377 --> 01:22:48,127
On the one hand, you have demonstrated
that this mission can be flown.

1044
01:22:48,207 --> 01:22:50,297
Perhaps the only way it can be survived.

1045
01:22:51,717 --> 01:22:53,427
On the other hand,

1046
01:22:53,507 --> 01:22:56,427
you did it by stealing
a multimillion-dollar military aircraft

1047
01:22:56,507 --> 01:22:59,387
and flying it in such a manner
that it may never be airworthy again.

1048
01:23:00,807 --> 01:23:03,097
Iceman is no longer here to protect you.

1049
01:23:03,937 --> 01:23:06,567
I have everything I need
to have you court-martialed

1050
01:23:06,647 --> 01:23:08,397
and dishonorably discharged.

1051
01:23:09,187 --> 01:23:10,567
So what do I do?

1052
01:23:11,567 --> 01:23:14,697
Risk the lives of my pilots
and perhaps the success of this mission

1053
01:23:16,197 --> 01:23:17,197
or...

1054
01:23:18,737 --> 01:23:20,197
risk my career

1055
01:23:21,287 --> 01:23:23,037
by appointing you team leader?

1056
01:23:26,377 --> 01:23:27,377
Sir--

1057
01:23:27,457 --> 01:23:31,087
I think the admiral's asking
a rhetorical question, Captain.

1058
01:25:11,938 --> 01:25:13,528
Talk to me, Goose.

1059
01:25:16,858 --> 01:25:18,358
Captain Mitchell!

1060
01:25:25,328 --> 01:25:26,998
You're where you belong.

1061
01:25:31,918 --> 01:25:33,418
Make us proud.

1062
01:25:59,528 --> 01:26:01,658
It has been an honor flying with you.

1063
01:26:02,738 --> 01:26:06,198
Each one of you represents
the best of the best.

1064
01:26:06,998 --> 01:26:09,708
This is a very specific mission.

1065
01:26:10,538 --> 01:26:13,838
My choice is a reflection of that
and nothing more.

1066
01:26:13,918 --> 01:26:15,748
Choose your two Foxtrot teams.

1067
01:26:17,338 --> 01:26:18,968
Payback and Fanboy.

1068
01:26:20,048 --> 01:26:21,388
Phoenix and Bob.

1069
01:26:25,678 --> 01:26:26,968
And your wingman.

1070
01:26:31,768 --> 01:26:32,768
Rooster.

1071
01:26:37,318 --> 01:26:39,608
The rest of you will stand by
on the carrier

1072
01:26:39,698 --> 01:26:42,568
for any reserve role that's required.

1073
01:26:43,448 --> 01:26:44,618
Dismissed.

1074
01:26:52,418 --> 01:26:55,248
Your target is a clear and present threat.

1075
01:26:56,748 --> 01:27:00,588
A secret uranium enrichment site
under rogue state control.

1076
01:27:01,218 --> 01:27:02,588
It's an underground bunker,

1077
01:27:02,678 --> 01:27:04,468
tucked between these two mountains.

1078
01:27:05,928 --> 01:27:09,728
Your route of ingress is heavily defended
by surface-to-air missiles

1079
01:27:09,808 --> 01:27:12,308
backed up by fifth-generation fighters.

1080
01:27:12,388 --> 01:27:15,148
Once your F-18 strike team
crosses the border,

1081
01:27:15,228 --> 01:27:17,228
Tomahawk missiles from the USS Leyte Gulf

1082
01:27:17,318 --> 01:27:20,938
will launch a synchronized strike
on the enemy's airfield here.

1083
01:27:22,238 --> 01:27:24,448
This will knock out their runway.

1084
01:27:26,238 --> 01:27:29,618
But you'll have to contend with
any planes already in the air.

1085
01:27:29,698 --> 01:27:32,538
The moment those Tomahawks hit,
the enemy will know you're coming.

1086
01:27:33,748 --> 01:27:37,788
Your time to target
will be two minutes and 30 seconds.

1087
01:27:39,458 --> 01:27:41,468
Any longer than that,
and you will be exposed

1088
01:27:41,548 --> 01:27:44,178
to any aircraft
the Tomahawks may have missed.

1089
01:27:47,548 --> 01:27:49,968
This is what you've all been training for.

1090
01:27:51,928 --> 01:27:53,438
Come home safely.

1091
01:28:08,118 --> 01:28:09,868
You give 'em hell!

1092
01:28:22,508 --> 01:28:23,508
Sir.

1093
01:28:24,008 --> 01:28:25,008
Sir?

1094
01:28:27,258 --> 01:28:28,258
I...

1095
01:28:31,178 --> 01:28:32,808
I just want to say--

1096
01:28:41,899 --> 01:28:43,239
We'll talk

1097
01:28:44,739 --> 01:28:46,109
when we get back.

1098
01:28:52,199 --> 01:28:53,999
Hey, Bradley! Bradley!

1099
01:28:55,119 --> 01:28:56,119
Hey.

1100
01:28:59,629 --> 01:29:01,039
You got this.

1101
01:29:09,469 --> 01:29:10,469
Maverick.

1102
01:29:12,719 --> 01:29:13,559
Maverick?

1103
01:29:15,519 --> 01:29:17,439
Hey, you with me?

1104
01:29:19,019 --> 01:29:20,859
I don't like that look, Mav.

1105
01:29:23,689 --> 01:29:25,189
It's the only one I got.

1106
01:29:29,819 --> 01:29:31,159
Thank you.

1107
01:29:32,659 --> 01:29:34,749
If I don't see you again, Hondo,

1108
01:29:34,829 --> 01:29:36,159
thank you.

1109
01:29:43,919 --> 01:29:45,759
It's been an honor, Captain.

1110
01:30:18,909 --> 01:30:21,959
Dagger One, up and ready on Catapult One.

1111
01:30:22,039 --> 01:30:24,169
Dagger Spare standing by.

1112
01:30:24,249 --> 01:30:26,049
Dagger Four, up and ready.

1113
01:30:26,129 --> 01:30:27,629
Dagger Three, up and ready.

1114
01:30:27,709 --> 01:30:29,839
Dagger Two, up and ready.

1115
01:30:31,009 --> 01:30:33,679
Support assets airborne.
Strike package ready.

1116
01:30:33,759 --> 01:30:35,639
Standing by for launch decision.

1117
01:30:36,269 --> 01:30:37,269
Send them.

1118
01:30:57,909 --> 01:30:59,199
Dagger Two away.

1119
01:31:00,209 --> 01:31:02,169
Dagger Three away.

1120
01:31:02,749 --> 01:31:04,169
Dagger Four away.

1121
01:31:15,179 --> 01:31:17,599
Comanche, Dagger One. Standby check in.

1122
01:31:18,969 --> 01:31:20,429
Comanche 11, set.

1123
01:31:20,519 --> 01:31:22,769
Picture clean. Recommend Dagger continue.

1124
01:31:22,849 --> 01:31:24,809
Copy. Daggers descending below radar.

1125
01:31:44,709 --> 01:31:47,379
Daggers now below radar.
Switching to E-2 picture.

1126
01:31:55,889 --> 01:31:58,469
Here we go. Enemy territory up ahead.

1127
01:31:58,559 --> 01:32:01,519
Feet dry in 60 seconds.
Comanche, Dagger One. Picture.

1128
01:32:01,599 --> 01:32:04,389
Comanche. Picture clean.
Decision is yours.

1129
01:32:04,479 --> 01:32:05,769
Copy.

1130
01:32:14,070 --> 01:32:15,200
Dagger attack.

1131
01:32:20,490 --> 01:32:21,790
Tomahawks airborne.

1132
01:32:21,870 --> 01:32:23,960
No turning back now.

1133
01:32:29,710 --> 01:32:31,760
Daggers, assume attack formation.

1134
01:32:40,850 --> 01:32:42,810
Daggers set. Proceeding to target.

1135
01:32:42,890 --> 01:32:47,440
Two minutes and 30 seconds
in three, two, one, mark.

1136
01:32:47,520 --> 01:32:48,860
-Two mark.
-Three mark.

1137
01:32:48,940 --> 01:32:49,820
Four mark.

1138
01:32:54,780 --> 01:32:55,700
Going in.

1139
01:33:11,340 --> 01:33:13,550
First SAM site overhead.

1140
01:33:17,930 --> 01:33:19,430
Looks like we're clear on radar, Mav.

1141
01:33:19,510 --> 01:33:21,260
Let's not take it for granted.

1142
01:33:24,770 --> 01:33:26,980
More SAMs! Three o'clock high!

1143
01:33:29,310 --> 01:33:31,690
-We got two minutes to target.
-Copy.

1144
01:33:31,770 --> 01:33:34,110
We're a few seconds behind, Rooster.
We got to move.

1145
01:33:35,650 --> 01:33:38,530
Thirty seconds to Tomahawk impact
on enemy airstrip.

1146
01:33:46,910 --> 01:33:47,920
Dagger, Comanche.

1147
01:33:48,000 --> 01:33:50,170
We're picking up two bandits.
Single group, two contacts.

1148
01:33:50,250 --> 01:33:53,000
-Where the hell'd they come from?
-Long-range patrol?

1149
01:33:58,010 --> 01:33:59,470
Comanche, what's their heading?

1150
01:33:59,550 --> 01:34:02,050
Bull's-eye 090, 50, tacked southwest.

1151
01:34:02,140 --> 01:34:04,220
They're headed away from us.
They don't know we're here.

1152
01:34:04,310 --> 01:34:06,270
The second those Tomahawks
hit the air base,

1153
01:34:06,350 --> 01:34:08,520
those bandits are gonna move
to defend the target.

1154
01:34:08,600 --> 01:34:11,190
We have to get there before they do.
Increase speed.

1155
01:34:12,560 --> 01:34:14,860
We got you, Mav. Don't wait for me.

1156
01:34:20,820 --> 01:34:23,830
Sir, Daggers Two and Four
are behind schedule.

1157
01:34:23,910 --> 01:34:25,910
Time to target, one minute 20.

1158
01:34:27,120 --> 01:34:29,290
Tomahawk impact in three, two...

1159
01:34:33,670 --> 01:34:36,130
Impact. Enemy runway is destroyed.

1160
01:34:36,920 --> 01:34:38,590
They know we're coming now.

1161
01:34:41,970 --> 01:34:44,300
Bandits are switching course
to defend the target.

1162
01:34:44,390 --> 01:34:45,510
Rooster, where are you?

1163
01:34:47,220 --> 01:34:48,980
Come on, Rooster. Bandits inbound.

1164
01:34:49,060 --> 01:34:51,230
We got to make up time now.
Let's turn and burn.

1165
01:34:59,190 --> 01:35:00,240
Heads up, Phoenix.

1166
01:35:10,040 --> 01:35:14,420
Sir, bandits are two minutes from target.
Daggers are one minute from target.

1167
01:35:14,500 --> 01:35:16,800
Come on, Rooster. Move it or lose it.

1168
01:35:19,050 --> 01:35:21,880
Guys, we're falling behind.
We really got to move.

1169
01:35:21,970 --> 01:35:23,759
If we don't increase our speed right now,

1170
01:35:23,839 --> 01:35:26,639
those bandits are gonna be waiting for us
when we reach the target.

1171
01:35:28,429 --> 01:35:29,639
Talk to me, Dad.

1172
01:35:30,979 --> 01:35:32,479
Come on, kid, you can do it.

1173
01:35:32,559 --> 01:35:34,609
Don't think, just do.

1174
01:35:43,109 --> 01:35:44,569
Jesus, Rooster, not that fast!

1175
01:35:44,659 --> 01:35:47,199
That's it, kid, that's it.
All right, let's go.

1176
01:35:51,289 --> 01:35:53,039
Damn, Rooster, take it easy.

1177
01:35:53,709 --> 01:35:56,339
Sir, Dagger Two is reengaging.

1178
01:35:56,419 --> 01:35:58,799
All right, now hit your target
and come home.

1179
01:36:03,219 --> 01:36:05,929
Thirty seconds to target.
Bob, check your laser.

1180
01:36:06,009 --> 01:36:09,519
Air-to-ground check complete.
Laser code verified, 1688.

1181
01:36:09,599 --> 01:36:10,679
Laser is a go!

1182
01:36:13,019 --> 01:36:14,389
Watch your heads.

1183
01:36:16,149 --> 01:36:17,609
Holy shit!

1184
01:36:17,689 --> 01:36:19,609
-Payback, you with me?
-Right behind you.

1185
01:36:20,689 --> 01:36:22,529
Phoenix, stand by for pop-up strike.

1186
01:36:22,609 --> 01:36:23,949
Dagger Three in position.

1187
01:36:24,609 --> 01:36:27,279
Popping in three, two, one.

1188
01:36:55,309 --> 01:36:57,559
-Get me eyes on that target, Bob.
-Dagger Three.

1189
01:36:58,439 --> 01:36:59,729
Stand by, Mav.

1190
01:36:59,819 --> 01:37:02,229
-Come on, Bob, come on.
-Stand by.

1191
01:37:02,819 --> 01:37:05,569
-I've got it. Captured!
-Target acquired. Bombs away.

1192
01:37:26,629 --> 01:37:30,009
We've got impact!
Check, direct hit! Direct hit!

1193
01:37:30,099 --> 01:37:31,929
That's miracle number one.

1194
01:37:32,599 --> 01:37:34,019
Dagger Two, status.

1195
01:37:34,099 --> 01:37:35,599
Almost there, Mav. Almost there.

1196
01:37:38,269 --> 01:37:39,859
Fanboy, where's my laser?

1197
01:37:40,439 --> 01:37:42,569
Rooster, there's something wrong
with this laser.

1198
01:37:42,649 --> 01:37:44,279
Shit! Deadeye, deadeye, deadeye!

1199
01:37:44,359 --> 01:37:46,699
Come on, guys, we're running out of time.
Get it online!

1200
01:37:46,779 --> 01:37:48,239
-I'm trying!
-Come on, Fanboy!

1201
01:37:48,319 --> 01:37:49,989
Nearly there! Nearly there!

1202
01:37:58,869 --> 01:38:01,459
-Come on, Fanboy, get it online.
-There's no time. I'm dropping blind.

1203
01:38:01,539 --> 01:38:03,749
-Rooster, I got this!
-No time. Pull up.

1204
01:38:03,839 --> 01:38:05,209
-Wait!
-Bombs away! Bombs away!

1205
01:38:18,768 --> 01:38:20,598
Bull's-eye, bull's-eye, bull's-eye!

1206
01:38:24,568 --> 01:38:25,858
Miracle number two.

1207
01:38:25,938 --> 01:38:27,568
Now they're in Coffin Corner.

1208
01:38:27,648 --> 01:38:29,738
We're not out of this yet.

1209
01:38:31,568 --> 01:38:32,988
Here it comes.

1210
01:38:36,038 --> 01:38:38,208
Radar warning! Smoke in the air.
Phoenix, break right.

1211
01:38:38,288 --> 01:38:40,578
Emergency jettison.
Dagger Three defending.

1212
01:38:40,668 --> 01:38:42,458
Here comes another one!

1213
01:38:42,538 --> 01:38:44,208
Dagger One defending.

1214
01:38:50,508 --> 01:38:51,588
Rooster, status.

1215
01:38:59,808 --> 01:39:00,808
Oh, my God.

1216
01:39:03,018 --> 01:39:04,438
Smoke in the air!

1217
01:39:05,818 --> 01:39:07,688
-Break right, Payback!
-Breaking right.

1218
01:39:09,108 --> 01:39:10,948
Oh, my God, here they come!

1219
01:39:11,028 --> 01:39:12,408
SAM on your six, Rooster!

1220
01:39:13,868 --> 01:39:15,238
Deploying countermeasures.

1221
01:39:18,078 --> 01:39:19,578
Negative contact.

1222
01:39:21,618 --> 01:39:22,708
Dagger One defending.

1223
01:39:24,128 --> 01:39:26,998
-Talk to me, Bob.
-Break right, Phoenix! Break right! Mav!

1224
01:39:27,088 --> 01:39:28,588
Nine o'clock! Nine o'clock!

1225
01:39:29,418 --> 01:39:31,378
Rooster, two more on your six.

1226
01:39:31,468 --> 01:39:32,928
Dagger Two, defending.

1227
01:39:37,508 --> 01:39:39,848
-Payback, SAM on your nose.
-Dagger Four defending.

1228
01:39:39,928 --> 01:39:41,518
-Rooster, tally, seven o'clock!
-Talk to me, Bob!

1229
01:39:41,598 --> 01:39:42,938
-On our six!
-Dagger Two defending.

1230
01:39:43,018 --> 01:39:44,688
-Phoenix, break right!
-I see it!

1231
01:39:52,068 --> 01:39:53,448
Dagger Two defending.

1232
01:39:54,818 --> 01:39:55,988
Shit, I'm out of flares!

1233
01:39:56,068 --> 01:39:58,408
Rooster, evade, evade!

1234
01:39:58,488 --> 01:40:00,748
I can't shake 'em!
They're on me! They're on me!

1235
01:40:10,878 --> 01:40:12,508
Mav! No!

1236
01:40:14,508 --> 01:40:18,008
Dagger One is hit!
I repeat, Dagger One is hit!

1237
01:40:18,098 --> 01:40:19,598
Maverick is down.

1238
01:40:19,678 --> 01:40:20,848
Dagger One, status.

1239
01:40:20,928 --> 01:40:22,558
Status!

1240
01:40:22,638 --> 01:40:24,768
Anyone see him? Does anyone see him?

1241
01:40:24,848 --> 01:40:27,058
-Dagger One, come in!
-I didn't see a parachute.

1242
01:40:27,188 --> 01:40:28,818
We have to circle back.

1243
01:40:28,898 --> 01:40:31,398
Comanche. Bandits inbound.
Single group, hot.

1244
01:40:31,488 --> 01:40:32,988
Recommend Dagger flow south.

1245
01:40:33,818 --> 01:40:35,818
One minute to intercept.

1246
01:40:39,078 --> 01:40:40,658
Get 'em back to the carrier now.

1247
01:40:40,738 --> 01:40:43,248
All Daggers flow to ECP.
You have bandits headed for you.

1248
01:40:43,328 --> 01:40:44,368
What about Maverick?

1249
01:40:44,458 --> 01:40:47,458
Tell him there's nothing he can do
for Maverick, not in a goddamn F-18.

1250
01:40:47,538 --> 01:40:50,378
Dagger Spare request permission
to launch and fly air cover.

1251
01:40:52,668 --> 01:40:53,667
Negative, Spare.

1252
01:40:54,837 --> 01:40:57,387
-Launch search and rescue.
-Negative. Not with bandits in the air.

1253
01:40:57,467 --> 01:41:01,007
-But, sir, Maverick is still out there.
-We are not losing anyone else today.

1254
01:41:02,977 --> 01:41:04,477
Get 'em home now.

1255
01:41:04,557 --> 01:41:07,097
Dagger, you are not to engage.

1256
01:41:07,187 --> 01:41:09,267
Repeat, do not engage.

1257
01:41:09,357 --> 01:41:12,437
Dagger Two, return to carrier.
Acknowledge.

1258
01:41:12,527 --> 01:41:13,527
Acknowledge.

1259
01:41:13,607 --> 01:41:17,067
Rooster, those bandits are closing.
We can't go back.

1260
01:41:17,157 --> 01:41:20,027
Rooster, he's gone.

1261
01:41:21,697 --> 01:41:23,197
Maverick's gone.

1262
01:42:53,667 --> 01:42:54,667
Oh, no, no.

1263
01:43:01,427 --> 01:43:02,887
Dagger Two is hit.

1264
01:43:04,047 --> 01:43:05,137
Dagger Two is hit.

1265
01:43:06,717 --> 01:43:08,097
Dagger Two, come in.

1266
01:43:09,807 --> 01:43:11,647
Dagger Two, do you copy?

1267
01:43:12,307 --> 01:43:14,607
Dagger Two, come in.

1268
01:43:39,876 --> 01:43:41,086
You all right?

1269
01:43:41,176 --> 01:43:42,756
Yeah, I'm good. You all right?

1270
01:43:45,346 --> 01:43:46,426
What the hell?

1271
01:43:46,506 --> 01:43:48,886
-What are you doing here?
-What am I doing here?

1272
01:43:48,966 --> 01:43:51,346
You think I took that missile
so you could be down here with me?

1273
01:43:51,436 --> 01:43:53,266
You should be back on the carrier by now!

1274
01:43:53,346 --> 01:43:55,056
I saved your life!

1275
01:43:55,186 --> 01:43:58,276
I saved your life. That's the whole point.

1276
01:43:58,356 --> 01:44:00,146
What the hell were you even thinking?

1277
01:44:00,236 --> 01:44:02,276
You told me not to think!

1278
01:44:18,996 --> 01:44:20,086
Well,

1279
01:44:21,416 --> 01:44:22,796
it's good to see you.

1280
01:44:25,216 --> 01:44:26,846
It's good to see you too.

1281
01:44:30,886 --> 01:44:32,346
So what's the plan?

1282
01:44:43,316 --> 01:44:44,696
You're not serious.

1283
01:45:00,206 --> 01:45:01,836
You've got to be shitting me.

1284
01:45:03,836 --> 01:45:04,876
An F-14?

1285
01:45:05,586 --> 01:45:07,386
I shot down three MiGs in one of those.

1286
01:45:07,466 --> 01:45:09,886
We don't even know
if that bag of ass can fly.

1287
01:45:12,596 --> 01:45:14,556
-Let's find out.
-Mav!

1288
01:45:16,436 --> 01:45:17,436
Okay.

1289
01:45:26,986 --> 01:45:28,986
-There's guys up there, Mav.
-Yeah.

1290
01:45:30,236 --> 01:45:32,156
-There's more over there.
-Okay.

1291
01:45:33,446 --> 01:45:35,616
-Let's start running.
-Yeah, run. Run.

1292
01:45:45,086 --> 01:45:47,466
Once I give you the signal for air,

1293
01:45:48,176 --> 01:45:50,886
you're gonna flip this switch
until the needle gets to 120.

1294
01:45:50,966 --> 01:45:52,136
When the engine starts,

1295
01:45:52,216 --> 01:45:54,726
you got to pull out the pins
and disconnect everything.

1296
01:45:54,806 --> 01:45:56,476
-You understand?
-Yeah.

1297
01:45:58,646 --> 01:45:59,646
Yes!

1298
01:46:01,516 --> 01:46:03,686
Once I'm up, stow the ladder.

1299
01:46:11,616 --> 01:46:13,656
Okay. Wow.

1300
01:46:14,826 --> 01:46:16,656
It's been a minute, huh, Mav?

1301
01:46:45,525 --> 01:46:48,485
Oh, my God. This thing is so old.

1302
01:46:49,485 --> 01:46:50,485
All right.

1303
01:46:55,575 --> 01:46:57,115
-Canopy?
-Clear.

1304
01:47:15,345 --> 01:47:17,215
Both runways are cratered.

1305
01:47:17,925 --> 01:47:20,015
How we gonna get this museum piece
in the air?

1306
01:47:30,395 --> 01:47:31,815
Why are the wings coming out, Mav?

1307
01:47:38,495 --> 01:47:41,205
Mav, this is a taxiway, not a runway.

1308
01:47:41,785 --> 01:47:44,705
This is a very short taxiway, Mav.

1309
01:47:44,785 --> 01:47:45,995
Just hang on.

1310
01:47:47,335 --> 01:47:48,705
Holy shit!

1311
01:47:54,755 --> 01:47:56,045
Come on, come on, come on.

1312
01:47:56,135 --> 01:47:57,175
Needle's alive.

1313
01:48:00,595 --> 01:48:02,845
-Mav?
-That's it. Come on, come on!

1314
01:48:02,935 --> 01:48:03,975
All right.

1315
01:48:04,895 --> 01:48:06,895
-Mav!
-Here we go.

1316
01:48:08,355 --> 01:48:09,775
Holy shit.

1317
01:48:23,535 --> 01:48:26,625
Sir, we're receiving a signal
from Rooster's ESAT.

1318
01:48:26,705 --> 01:48:28,625
But there seems to be a malfunction.

1319
01:48:28,705 --> 01:48:30,045
-Have you lost him?
-No, sir.

1320
01:48:31,045 --> 01:48:32,505
He's supersonic.

1321
01:48:33,125 --> 01:48:34,215
He's airborne.

1322
01:48:35,465 --> 01:48:37,045
-In what?
-Sir.

1323
01:48:37,755 --> 01:48:42,015
Overwatch reports an F-14 Tomcat is
airborne and on course for our position.

1324
01:48:42,935 --> 01:48:45,475
Can't be. It can't be!

1325
01:48:47,185 --> 01:48:48,185
Maverick.

1326
01:48:50,435 --> 01:48:52,775
Okay, Rooster,
get us in touch with the boat.

1327
01:48:52,855 --> 01:48:54,315
I'm working on it.

1328
01:48:54,395 --> 01:48:57,815
Radio's out. No radar.
Everything's dead back here.

1329
01:48:58,485 --> 01:49:00,865
-What do I do? Talk me through it.
-Okay, first the radio.

1330
01:49:00,945 --> 01:49:02,115
Throw the...

1331
01:49:02,955 --> 01:49:05,165
the UHF-2 circuit breaker.

1332
01:49:05,245 --> 01:49:06,245
Try that.

1333
01:49:06,825 --> 01:49:09,285
There's 300 breakers back here.
Anything more specific?

1334
01:49:09,375 --> 01:49:11,335
I don't know.
That was your dad's department.

1335
01:49:11,415 --> 01:49:12,874
I'll figure it out.

1336
01:49:16,214 --> 01:49:18,214
Mav, tally two, 5:00 low.

1337
01:49:23,724 --> 01:49:24,844
What do we do?

1338
01:49:25,514 --> 01:49:27,644
Okay, listen. Just be cool.

1339
01:49:27,724 --> 01:49:29,684
If they knew who we were,
we'd be dead already.

1340
01:49:32,064 --> 01:49:34,024
Well, here they come.

1341
01:49:34,694 --> 01:49:37,194
-What's your plan?
-Just put your mask on.

1342
01:49:38,444 --> 01:49:40,774
Remember, we're on the same team.

1343
01:49:43,494 --> 01:49:45,284
Just wave and smile.

1344
01:49:45,904 --> 01:49:47,534
Just wave and smile.

1345
01:49:54,664 --> 01:49:56,464
What's that signal? What's he saying?

1346
01:49:56,544 --> 01:49:59,424
No idea. I have no idea what he's saying.

1347
01:50:00,294 --> 01:50:03,674
-What about that one? Any idea?
-No, never seen that one either.

1348
01:50:07,014 --> 01:50:10,804
Oh, shit. His wingman is moving
into weapons envelope.

1349
01:50:11,644 --> 01:50:13,184
All right, listen up.

1350
01:50:13,274 --> 01:50:15,984
When I tell you,
you grab those rings above your head.

1351
01:50:16,064 --> 01:50:17,644
That's the ejection handle.

1352
01:50:18,734 --> 01:50:20,904
Mav, can we outrun these guys?

1353
01:50:21,574 --> 01:50:23,284
Not their missiles and guns.

1354
01:50:28,284 --> 01:50:29,664
Then it's a dogfight.

1355
01:50:30,374 --> 01:50:33,204
An F-14 against fifth-gen fighters?

1356
01:50:34,754 --> 01:50:36,964
It's not the plane, it's the pilot.

1357
01:50:38,544 --> 01:50:40,504
You'd go after 'em if I wasn't here.

1358
01:50:41,174 --> 01:50:42,844
But you are here.

1359
01:50:43,634 --> 01:50:44,964
Come on, Mav.

1360
01:50:46,094 --> 01:50:47,264
Don't think.

1361
01:50:48,554 --> 01:50:49,594
Just do.

1362
01:51:05,234 --> 01:51:07,194
Tell me when you see smoke in the air.

1363
01:51:11,574 --> 01:51:13,664
-Smoke in the air! Smoke in the air!
-Hang on.

1364
01:51:16,504 --> 01:51:19,004
Yeah, Mav! Splash one! Splash one!

1365
01:51:24,344 --> 01:51:25,554
Here comes another one.

1366
01:51:28,804 --> 01:51:30,844
Rooster, flares! Now, now, now!

1367
01:51:34,264 --> 01:51:35,514
Splitting the throttles.

1368
01:51:37,684 --> 01:51:38,814
Coming around.

1369
01:51:43,154 --> 01:51:45,614
-Give me tone, give me tone.
-You got him, Mav! You got him!

1370
01:51:45,694 --> 01:51:46,614
Taking the shot.

1371
01:51:53,284 --> 01:51:54,534
What the--

1372
01:51:55,534 --> 01:51:57,664
Holy shit! What the fuck was that?

1373
01:51:59,084 --> 01:52:01,334
Hang on. We got to get low.

1374
01:52:01,424 --> 01:52:03,713
The terrain will confuse
his targeting system.

1375
01:52:05,843 --> 01:52:06,753
Here he comes!

1376
01:52:19,563 --> 01:52:21,483
Talk to me, Rooster. Where is he?

1377
01:52:21,563 --> 01:52:23,233
He's still on us!

1378
01:52:30,403 --> 01:52:32,493
-We took a hit! We took a hit!
-Damn it!

1379
01:52:37,583 --> 01:52:40,003
-Come on, Mav. Do some of that pilot shit.
-Brace yourself.

1380
01:52:50,463 --> 01:52:51,513
Holy shit.

1381
01:52:58,563 --> 01:53:00,393
I got tone. Taking the shot.

1382
01:53:04,853 --> 01:53:06,103
Damn it!

1383
01:53:07,113 --> 01:53:09,363
Out of missiles. Switching to guns.

1384
01:53:15,703 --> 01:53:16,823
Come on, Mav, come on.

1385
01:53:19,493 --> 01:53:21,123
-You got him, Mav!
-It's not over yet.

1386
01:53:25,833 --> 01:53:27,673
-One last chance.
-You can do this.

1387
01:53:28,843 --> 01:53:30,053
Come on, Maverick.

1388
01:53:40,143 --> 01:53:42,063
Yes! Splash two!

1389
01:53:53,113 --> 01:53:55,033
-Mav, I got the radio on.
-Outstanding.

1390
01:53:55,113 --> 01:53:57,073
-Get us in touch with the boat.
-Copy that.

1391
01:53:59,283 --> 01:54:00,493
Oh, my God.

1392
01:54:02,493 --> 01:54:04,164
Where the hell is this guy?

1393
01:54:05,504 --> 01:54:07,084
He's on our nose.

1394
01:54:10,504 --> 01:54:11,714
Damn it, we're out of ammo.

1395
01:54:13,844 --> 01:54:16,184
Smoke in the air! Rooster, flares!

1396
01:54:18,724 --> 01:54:20,014
That was close.

1397
01:54:22,474 --> 01:54:24,394
We're out of flares, Mav.

1398
01:54:28,604 --> 01:54:30,564
Shit, he's already on us.

1399
01:54:35,404 --> 01:54:37,114
This is not good.

1400
01:54:45,294 --> 01:54:47,254
-We took another hit!
-No, no, no!

1401
01:54:52,044 --> 01:54:54,344
We can't take much more of this.

1402
01:54:54,424 --> 01:54:56,174
We can't outrun this guy. We got to eject.

1403
01:54:56,264 --> 01:54:57,514
-What?
-We need altitude.

1404
01:54:57,594 --> 01:54:59,304
Pull the ejection handles
the second I tell you.

1405
01:54:59,384 --> 01:55:01,854
-Mav, wait!
-Rooster, there's no other way.

1406
01:55:05,104 --> 01:55:06,684
Eject, eject, eject!

1407
01:55:07,524 --> 01:55:09,564
Rooster, pull the handle! Eject!

1408
01:55:09,654 --> 01:55:11,234
It's not working.

1409
01:55:21,915 --> 01:55:23,245
Mav!

1410
01:55:25,585 --> 01:55:26,915
I'm sorry.

1411
01:55:28,415 --> 01:55:29,925
I'm sorry, Goose.

1412
01:55:42,645 --> 01:55:46,645
Good afternoon, ladies and gentlemen.
This is your savior speaking.

1413
01:55:46,725 --> 01:55:48,275
Please fasten your seat belts,

1414
01:55:48,355 --> 01:55:51,405
return your tray tables
to their locked and upright positions

1415
01:55:52,355 --> 01:55:54,615
and prepare for landing.

1416
01:55:56,945 --> 01:55:59,195
Hey, Hangman, you look good.

1417
01:55:59,285 --> 01:56:02,615
I am good, Rooster. I'm very good.

1418
01:56:04,495 --> 01:56:06,205
I'll see you back on deck.

1419
01:56:28,106 --> 01:56:29,566
Maverick is downwind.

1420
01:56:29,646 --> 01:56:33,106
No front landing gear. No tailhook.
Pull the cable and raise the barricade.

1421
01:56:33,196 --> 01:56:35,276
Foul deck! Raise the barricade!

1422
01:56:36,366 --> 01:56:37,736
Go!

1423
01:57:00,266 --> 01:57:02,386
Please don't tell me we lost an engine.

1424
01:57:02,476 --> 01:57:05,096
-All right, I won't tell you that.
-Okay.

1425
01:57:28,877 --> 01:57:29,797
You good?

1426
01:57:30,547 --> 01:57:32,207
Yeah. I'm good.

1427
01:58:17,887 --> 01:58:20,387
-Chalked yourself another kill.
-That makes two.

1428
01:58:21,137 --> 01:58:23,927
Mav has five. Makes him an ace.

1429
01:58:42,158 --> 01:58:44,328
Captain Mitchell! Captain Mitchell!

1430
01:58:51,168 --> 01:58:52,418
Sir.

1431
01:59:00,008 --> 01:59:01,638
Thank you for saving my life.

1432
01:59:03,058 --> 01:59:04,928
It's what my dad would've done.

1433
01:59:44,178 --> 01:59:45,179
Hey, Mav.

1434
01:59:46,269 --> 01:59:47,349
Jimmy.

1435
01:59:48,559 --> 01:59:49,559
Is...

1436
01:59:50,479 --> 01:59:51,979
Is Penny around?

1437
01:59:52,059 --> 01:59:55,319
She took Amelia on a sailing trip.

1438
01:59:57,899 --> 02:00:00,149
Did she say when she'd be back?

1439
02:00:00,239 --> 02:00:01,739
You know, she didn't.

1440
02:00:04,069 --> 02:00:05,739
Can I get you anything?

1441
02:00:19,169 --> 02:00:20,089
Get in there.